  FT["PH-H18757"] = {"id":"PH-H18757","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ORGANIZING THE MUNICIPAL DISTRICT OF KAPA- TAGAN, PROVINCE OF LANAO, INTO A REGU- LAR MUNICIPALITY.","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES ORGANIZING THE MUNICIPAL DISTRICT OF KAPA- TAGAN, PROVINCE OF LANAO, INTO A REGU- LAR MUNICIPALITY."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 237","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00237_1949.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00237_1949.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18757-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"The municipality of Kapatagan as herein organized shall\nbegin to exist upon appointment and qualification of the\nMayor, the Vice-Mayor and a majority of the councilors\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of July, in\nthe year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-nine,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the fourth.\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nTEODORO EVAngELISTA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18758"] = {"id":"PH-H18758","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALAG AÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"MALAG AÑANG RESIDENCE OF THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 237","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00237_1957.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00237_1957.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18758-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"The following symbols for the various commissioned\ngrades are hereby established:\n0-6 - Colonel or Navy Coptain\n0-5 - Lieutenant Colonel or Commander\n0-4 - Mojor or Lieutenont Commander\n0-3 - Coptain or Lieutenant, Senior Grade\n0-2 - First Lieutenont or Lieutenont, Junior Grade\n0-1 - Second Lieuteront or Ensign\nThe Corps of Professors promotion list shall be\nestoblished in accordonce with the followings\n\n- 2 -\n(a) The nomes of all officers of the Corps of Professors\nshall be carried in this list which shall estoblish permonently\nthe relative seniority of such officers, subject to the exceptions\nprovided for in Section 9(e) hereof: Provided, That the Corps of\nProfessors promotion list as of Januory 10, 1956, as amended, shall\nbe the bosis of all subsequent lists that may be mode in complionce\nwith this Order.\nThe nomes of all officers of this list shall be orranged\nby grade in the following order: First, , 0-6; second, , 0-5; third,\n, 0-3.\nAmong officers of the some grode, the officer\nwhose nome appears first on such list shall be the senior, the offi-\ncer whose nome appears second on the list shall be the senior next\nbelow the first, the officer whose name appears third on the list\nsholl be the senior next below the second, and so on throughout\n(c) Officers hereafter appointed in the Corps of Professors\npromotion list sholl be inserted therein as provided for in Section\n8 of this Order.\n(a) The Chief of Stoff shall couse all changes occasioned by\nseporations, appointments, promotions, loss of rank by action of\ncourt-martial, and oll other changes due to operation of low or re-\ngulotions to be entered on the approved Corps of Professors promotion\nlist, and as corrected, this list sholl be published to the Armed\nForces ot least once ech year.\nThere shall be designated from among the members of\nthe Corps of Professors the Dean of the Corps of Professors who\nshall be senior in ocademic rank and military grade to all other\nmembers of the Corps of Professors.\nThe academic ranks of the other\nmembers of the Corps of Professors shall. be, in descending order;\nprofessor, associate professor, and assistant professor."}},{"id":"PH-H18758-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"For each academic department of the Philippine Military\nAcademy, a member of the Corps of Professors sholl be designated the\nHead thereof who shall be senior to all other members of the Corps\nof Professors in thot academic department. For each course of\ninstruction prescribed in the approved academic curriculum of the\nPhilippine Military Acodemy, there may be only one member of the\nCorpse 6 Brat Barre or thated,. *hich officer shall be desirnated\nThe initial appointment of members of the Corps of\nProfessors sholl be made in accordance with the following:\n(a) Members of the Corps of Professors sholl be initiolly ap-\npointed in on academic rank and in a corresponding military grade\n\n= 3 -\nby the President of the Philippines upon recommendation of the Chief\nof Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines: Provided, That no applicant\nshall be initially appointed in the academic rank of professor or\nassociate professor who does not possess a doctor's degree or a\nmoster's degree, respectively, from an occredited shall in the\nfield of study for which he is to be appointed.\nCommissioned officers of the Armed Forces of the Philip-\npines may be appointed to the Corps of Professors upon their own\napplication, in which case, except as hereinofter provided in\nparograph (c) of this Section, they shall be appointed in the some\ncommissioned grades they held on the date of such appointment:\nProvided, That nothing in this Order sholl prevent the Chief of\nStoff from detoiling for specified periods such officers of the\nArmed Forces who are qualified to occupy the position of instructor\nin the academic foculty of the Philippine Military Academy.\nthus assigned by the Chief of Stoff to the acodemic faculty of the\nPhilippine Military Acodemy sholl not, by virtue of such assignment,\nbe seporated from their assigned orms and services and shall not be\nsubject to the rules ond regulations prescribed herein for members\nof the Corps of Professors.\n(c) Officers initiolly appointed in the following academic\nranks shall be concurrently appointed in the corresponding grade\ninficated, if they hold a lower made at the time of their oppoint-\n(1)\n(2)\nAssociate professor\n(3)\nAssistant professor\n0-5\n0-4\n0-3\nOfficers hereafter appointed in the Corps of Professors\npromotion list shall be inserted therein os follows:\nAn officer appointed in a grade higher than the commissioned\ngrode he hold ot the time of his appointment sholl be placed at the\nbottom of officers of the grode in which appointed.\nAn officer appointed in the same commissioned grade he\nheld ot the time of his appointment shall be placed immediately below\nthe most junior officer of that grode who has the same or longer ac-\ncumulated service in such grade: Provided, That the accumulated\nservice in grode referred to herein shall be construed to mean the\nsum total of the active service rendered in such permanent grade in\nthe Regulor Force and/or Reserve Force: Provided, further, That for\npurposes of determining the initial placement of officers covered\nby this Section ond for purposes of effecting the promotions in\nmilitary grade prescribed in Sections 9(a), 9(b), and 9(c) hereof,\nofficers who render service in the Corps of Professors as an acting\n\n4 -\nprofessor, acting associote professor, or acting assistant pro-\nfessor, and who are subsequently appointed therein, respectively,\nin the academic rank of professor and in the grade of 0-5, in\nthe academic rank of associate professor and in the grade of 0-4,\nand in the acodemic rank of assistant professor and in the grade\nof 0-3, shall have such service credited as octive service rendered\nin the grade of 0-5,\n0-4, and 0-3, respectively."}},{"id":"PH-H18758-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 9"},"text":{"en":"Members of the Corps of Professors shall be promoted\nin military grade and in academic ronk in accordance with the follow-\ning rules and regulations:\n(a) Officers initially appointed in the academic rank of pro-\nfessor and in the grade of 0-5 sholl be promoted to the grade of\n0-6 unon completion of eight years of accumulated active commissioned\nservice in the grade of 0-5:\nProvided, That they shall have rendered\nat least six yeors of satisfoctory service in the Corps of Professors.\nThe grade of 0-6 shall be the highest permanent or temporary grade\nin the acodemic rank of professor, and promotions to this grode sholl\nbe subject to the confirmation of the Commission on Appointments.\n(b) Officers initiolly appointed in the acodemic rank of asso-\nciate professor and in the grade of 0-4 shall be promoted to the\ngrade of 0-5 upon completion of seven yers of accumulated active\ncommissioned service in the grade of 0-4: Provided, That they shall\nhave rendered at least five years of satisfoctory service in the\nCorps of Professors, The grade of 0-5 shall be the highest permonent\nor temporory grade in the academic rank of associate professor,\nassociate professor who is promoted in academic rank to professor\nsholl also be promoted to the next higher military grole on the\neffective date of promotion in academic rank regardless of the\nlength of service in grode if he is in the grade of 0-4, or upon\ncompletion of seven vers accumulated service in the grade of 0-5\nwith ot leost six yeors of sotisfactory service in the Corps of\nProfessors.\n(c) Officers initially appointed in the academic rank of as-\nsistant professor ond in the grade of 0-3 shall be promoted to the\ngrade of 0-4 upon completion of five years of accumulated active\ncommissioned service in the grade of 0-3: Provided, That they shall\nhove rendered ot least four years of sotisfactory service in the\nCorps of Professors.\nThe erode of 0-4 shall be the highest permanent\nor temporory grade in the academic rank of assistant professor.\nassistant professor who is promoted in academic rank to associate\nprofessor shall also be promoted to the next higher military grade\non the effective dote of promotion in acodemic rank regordless of\nthe length of service in grade if he is in the grade of 0-3, or upon\ncomletion of six years accumulated service in the grade of 0-4 with\nat leost five yeors service in the Corps of Professors.\n\n(a) When an officer in any grode is promoted to the next\nhigher prode under the provisions of sections 9(a), 9(b), or\n9(c) of this Order, all officers of the some grade and the\nsome academic rank who ore senior to such officer, notwith-\nstanding the promotionol requirements prescribed in said Sec-\ntions, shall also be promoted to the next higher grade together\nwith such officer, if found qualified therefor by the Corps of\nProfessors promotion board,\n(e) The Dean of the Corps of Professors ond the heals of\nacademic departments shall be designated by the Chief of Staff\nupon recommendation of the Superintendent of the Philippine Mili-\ntary Academy. Any member of the Corps of Professors who shall be\ndesignated as Dean of the Corps of Professors whenever vacancy in\nthat position exists sholl be promoted in grade or advonced in\nseniority, whichever sholl be necessory to give him seniority over\nall other members of the Corps of Professors, irrespective of his\nlength of service in grade.\nLikewise, any member of the Corps of\nProfessors who sholl be designated as the Head of an acodemic de-\npartment whenever vacancy in that position exists shall be promoted\nin militory grade or alvanced in seniority, whichever sholl cive him\nseniority over all other members of the Corps of Professors basically\nassigned to that academic department, irrespective of his length of\nservice in grade: Provided, That the promotions of officers in grade\ncontemplated under this poragraph sholl not result in exceeding the\nhighest commissioned grade authorized for their respective scademic\nranks: Provided, further, That those designated as Dean, Corps of\nProfessors, and Heads of academic departments sholl have served, on\nthe date of designation, ot leost five years and three years, res-\npectively, as members of the Corps of Professors.\n(f) A board of officers to be appointed by the Chief of Staff\nfor a term of two years shall meet at least once annually to consider\nthe elicibility of any members of the Corps of Professors for promotion\nin academic rank ond sholl submit appropriate recommendations thereon\nto the Chief of Stoff.\nSaid board shall consist of the Dean of the\nCorps of Professors and at least four other members, not members of\nthe Corps of Professors, who shall be senior in permonent grade and\ntemporary grade to any officer being considered by their board.\nRecommendations for promotion in academic rank shall be based on a\ncareful consideration ond evaluation of the condidate's academic\nond militory qualifications, experience, performance of duty, present\nassignment, potentiality to the service, specific recommendations of\nthe academic department heads concerned whenever applicable, and such\nother factors as may be deemed pertinent by the board. Promotions in\nacademic rank shall be made only upon recommendation of this boord as\nOpproved by the Chief of Staff.\n\n- 6 -\n(g) Promotions in grade sholl be subject to the approval of\nthe President of the Philippines,\nPromotions to grades as in-\ndicated in porographs (a), (b), (c), (a) and (e) of this Section\nsholl be recommended by a promotion board composed of ot least\nfive officers who ore not members of the Corps of Professors and\nwho shall be oppointed by the Secretory of National Defense for\na term of one veor.\nThe operation of and recommendations made\nbw this board shall be subiect to the provisions of Sections\nof Republic Act No. 291.\nSaid boord shall also be empowered to\ndefer for promotion any officer whom the boord deems is not fully\nquolified for promotion, notwithstanding his completion of the\nservice-in-grade requirements prescribed in porographs (a), (b),\nand (c) of this Section. Whenever any officer is thus deferred,\nthe provisions of Sections 7(e) and 7(f) of Republic Act No. 291\nshall apply.\n(h) For purposes of promotion in academic ronk and in commis-\nsioned grode, satisfoctory service rendered in the grade of at least\n0-3 as o member of the acodemic foculty of the Philippine Military\nAcodemy sholl be credited as service rendered in the Corps of Pro-\nfessors: Provided, That the amount of service thot may thus be credited\nshall not exceed four years."}},{"id":"PH-H18758-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 10"},"text":{"en":"Any member of the Corps of Professors who sholl\ndemonstrate on outstonding performance in ony field of activity\nof the acodemic foculty of the Philippine Military Academy may be\ntemporarily promoted, upon recommendation of the Dean of the Corps\nof Professors, through the Superintendent, irrespective of his length\nof service in grade, to the next higher military grode without vocoting\nhis permonent rade:\nProvided, Thot this temporory promotion sholl not\nresult in exceeding the maximum militory grode for his academic rank.\nExcept os hereinbefcre provided, members of the Corps\nof Professors sholl be given the same pay, allowances,\nretirement privileges, and the like to which regulor officers are\nAssociote professors and assistant professors who are not\nadvonced in acodemic rank ofter completing nine ond seven yeors, res-\npectively, in such academic ronks sholl be separated from the service\nwithout prejudice to seporation or retirement benefits provided for\nin Republic Act No. 340.\nIn time of wor or at ony time the President of the\nPhilippines may declare a national emergency, any member of the Corps\nof Professors whose services shall be needed to corry out the mission\nof the Armed Forces may be detailed with such orms or services where\nhe is best quolified at the discretion of the President.\nsituation would not worrant the continuous operation of the Philippine\n\n7 -\nMilitary Academy, all members of the Corps of Professors shall\nbe detailed to such arms and services where they are best quali-\nfied: Provided, That no transfers of members of the Corps of\nProfessors to any other arm, bronch, service or promotion list\nshall be permitted.\nExecutive Orders Nos. 361 and 643 dated August 6, 1941,\nand November 21, 1953, respectively, ore hereby revoked.\nthe Independence of the Philippines, the eleventh.\n(SGD.) RAMON MAGSAYSAY\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) FORTUNATO DE LEON\nExecutive Secretory"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18759"] = {"id":"PH-H18759","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_237_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating the National Council for Small and Medium Industries","orig":"Creating the National Council for Small and Medium Industries"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 237","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-06-16","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00237_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00237_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18759-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"Functions and Duties. – The Council shall have the following functions and duties:\na) To make studies on and integrate all proposed measures relative to the promotion and development of small\nand medium industries;\nb) To propose and adopt policies, objectives and priorities affecting small and medium industries;\nc) To formulate a credit program for small and medium industries for government financial institutions and\nfollow up its implementation by said institutions;\nd) To coordinate and integrate the activities of all government agencies relative to small and medium\nindustries to the end that all efforts may be effectively channeled to the objective of attaining the promotion\nand development of small and medium industries; and\ne) To undertake such other measures as may be necessary to the attainment of the objectives herein\nestablished."}},{"id":"PH-H18759-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"Council Secretariat. – The U.P. Institute for Small-Scale Industries shall be the Secretariat of the\nCouncil. The Chairman of the Council may request the detail of such additional personnel from other\ngovernment agencies as may be required."}},{"id":"PH-H18759-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Meetings and Reports. – The Council shall meet at such times as may be determined by the\nChairman and shall render to the President of the Philippines period and annual reports of its activities."}},{"id":"PH-H18759-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Funding. – Operating expenses of the Council shall be chargeable against the annual\nappropriation for the U.P. Institute for Small-Scale Industries. Additional expenses as may be necessary shall\nbe chargeable against other available funds of the government."}},{"id":"PH-H18759-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"All Departments, bureaus, offices, agencies and instrumentalities of the government, including\ngovernment-owned or controlled corporations, and local governments shall extend assistance to the Council\nwhenever the Council shall need and request such assistance."}},{"id":"PH-H18759-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity of the Order. – This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 16th day of June, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and seventy.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\nActing Executive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18760"] = {"id":"PH-H18760","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG REORGANIZING THE CABINET SECRETARIAT AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"MALACAÑANG REORGANIZING THE CABINET SECRETARIAT AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 237","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00237_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00237_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18760-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"topics for the\nCabinet deliberations,\ndiscussion of Cabinet meetings.\nor facilitate the\nPowers and Functions.\nTo carry out its mandate,\nthe Cabinet Secretariat shall have the following powers and\nassist in providing timely and organized information\nto the Cabinet on issues and problems submitted for decision and\naction; provide conference and administrative support services to\nthe cabinet, the Cabinet Clusters, .the Cabinet Assistance System\nand other committees created by the cabinet; at the instance of\nthe Cabinet, conduct technical research and special studies on\nspecific policy issues; maintain an efficient records management\nsystem including a Cabinet Archives and a library; certify\nCabinet resolutions that indicate agreements and actions reached\nduring Cabinet meetings; and exercise such other functions and\npowers as may be provided by law or as directed by the President.\nStructural Organization. The Cabinet Secretariat\nshall be headed by a Cabinet Secretary, assisted by one Cabinet\nUndersecretary.\nThe Cabinet\nSecretary and the Cabinet\nUndersecretary, who shall have the rank of a Secretary and\nUndersecretary, respectively,\nshall be appointed by the\nThere shall be two\n(2) Staffs namely, the Technical\nAffairs Staff and the Conference Affairs Staff, each to be\nheaded by a Presidential staff Director appointed by the\nPresident upon the recommendation of the Cabinet Secretary.\nThe Cabinet Secretary is hereby authorized to delineate and\nassign the respective functional areas of responsibilities of the\nThe Cabinet Secretary shall ensure\nthat only highly-qualified technical and professional people will\nbe appointed.\nTo the extent possible, subject to qualification\nstandards to be prescribed by the Cabinet Secretary, the Cabinet\nSecretariat shall draw its personnel from the existing Cabinet\nSecretariat in the Office of the President.\nNew structure and Pattern.\nUpon approval of this\nExecutive Order, the officers and employees of the Cabinet\nSecretariat shall, in\nhold-over capacity, continue to perform\ntheir respective duties and responsibilities and receive the\ncorresponding salaries and benefits.\nThe new position structure and staffing pattern of the\nCabinet Secretariat shall be approved and prescribed by the\nCabinet Secretary within one hundred and twenty (120) days from\nthe approval of this Executive Order and the authorized positions\ncreated thereunder shall be filled with regular appointments by\nhim or by the President as the case maybe.\nThose incumbents\nwhose positions are not included therein or who\nreappointed shall be deemed separated from the service.\nseparated from the service shall receive the retirement benefits\nto which they may be entitled under existing laws, rules and\nregulations.\notherwise, they shall be paid the equivalent of one\n(1) month basic salary for every year of service in the\ngovernment, or the equivalent nearest fraction thereof favorable\nto them on the basis of the highest salary received, but in no\ncase shall such payment exceed the equivalent of twelve (12)\nmonths of salary.\nAll applicable appropriations and\nplantilla items of the Cabinet Secretariat in the defunct Office\nof the Prime Minister and of the then Cabinet standing Committee\nare hereby transferred to the Cabinet Secretariat.\nTransfer of Records, Assets and Equipment.\napplicable records,\nassets and equipment of the Cabinet\nSecretariat in the defunct office of the Prime Minister and of\nthe then Cabinet Standing Committee are hereby transferred to the\nCabinet Secretariat.\nAssistance to the Cabinet Secretary.\nCabinet Secretary may call upon the assistance of any department,\nbureau, office, agency, committee,\ninstrumentality of the government as may be needed.\nSeparability.\nAny portion or provision of this\nExecutive Order that may be declared unconstitutional shall not\nhave the effect of nullifying other portions or provisions hereof\nas long as such remaining portions or provisions can still\nsubsist and be given effect in their entirety.\nRepealing Clauso.\nAll laws, ordinances, rules,\nregulations and other issuances or parts thereof, which are\ninconsistent with this Executive Order, are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly.\nEffectivity.\neffect immediately upon its approval.\nThis Executive Order shall take\nEighty-Seven.\nCity o1 Manila,\nin the Year of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and\nfortage do. Aguir\nBy the President:\nJOKER P: ARROYO\néxecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
