  FT["PH-H18884"] = {"id":"PH-H18884","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"PMS LIBRARY /:\\DDRESSI~G Rl:RAL POVER11- I~ l'HE PHILIPPli~ES THROL\"GH THE CONSEI{V r\\1l0N, PROTECTION DEVELOP~IE.~T","orig":"PMS LIBRARY /:\\DDRESSI~G Rl:RAL POVER11- I~ l'HE PHILIPPli~ES THROL\"GH THE CONSEI{V r\\1l0N, PROTECTION DEVELOP~IE.~T"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 255","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00255_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00255_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18884-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"T., JOSEPH FJERCITO ESTRADA, President of the\nRepublic of tile Philippines, by ~irtue of the po\\vers vested in me by law, do hereby declare\ntile establishJnent of a net\\vork of collunwUty-based enteJ1Jrises to address rllfal poverty\nthrOUgll the consen'ation, protection and development of natllfal resotlfCes.\nS~clion 1. ~ el,vork. Tl1e ~ ,'\\PC shall I a}. tile groundwork fOJ: tile establislunent of a\nne~vork of local government tmits \"lth\ncommlullt}..based enteI1)rises implementing\n:':-\"'_\".~':'\n,'-;---':\\;\n,\n-==\n/~-.,.,.:-:.\n\". .\n;:',;\n.\n:~~;\n:\n\"\n.\n..\n........\n..\n.\n.\n.....\n....\n...\n..\nVice-Chairrnill1\nNAPC NGO Sector Representative\nD ILG Representative\nDE.'iR Representative\nDA Representative\nFam1er Sector Represen~lrjvc\nFisherfolk Sector RepreseIl~ltive\n,\n'--'-\n~,\n.\nIII/III/IIIII/II!II!m:18291\n\"ecrion 7, Endowment Flmd. A poftjon of the NPGA CVF shall be set aside as an\nendo\\vment fwId for the benefit of ~GOs and pas irnplementing community-based\nenterprises through the conservation, protection and development of natural resources,\nespeciall}' tllose leading to biodiversity conservation and sustainable development. This sum\nmay be added to an existing environmental endowment fund; provided, that the earnings\nfrom this contribution shall be administered separately from otller funds, subject to such\nadministrative agreements as may be agreed upon when the contribution is effected,\nReQealinv.. and SeQarabili!;'y Clause. This Order modifies, repeals,\namends, revokes all previous issuances, orders, circulars inconsistent herewith. Uncontested\nprovisions shall remain valid and binding should some p:.U1S herein be declared\nW1constitutional.\nThis Order tlkes effect immediately.\nDone in Manila, this ~\nJc JIYIi!J-in the )\"ear of Our Lord, Twenty\n..\n1':~\"'-1\"\nPJEE Hologram ~ 8292\n...\n....... .\n....\n....\n,\n.....\nBy the President:\nRonalda B. Zamora\n~~.~~~"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18885"] = {"id":"PH-H18885","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY CREATING THE OFFICE OF A PRESIDENTIAL ADVISER UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT TO IMPLEMENT THE RECOMMENDATIONS OF THE FELICIANO COMMISSION","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY CREATING THE OFFICE OF A PRESIDENTIAL ADVISER UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT TO IMPLEMENT THE RECOMMENDATIONS OF THE FELICIANO COMMISSION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 255","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00255_2003.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00255_2003.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18885-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Creation and Mandate. There is hereby created an Office of\na Presidential Adviser under the Office of the President to implement the\nrecommendations of the Feliciano Commission."}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"Duties and Functions. The Presidential Adviser shall have\nthe following duties and functions:\nEnsure the institutionalization and monitoring of reform measures in\nthe organizations of the Department of National Defense (DND) and\nthe Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP).\nConduct a comprehensive study on the areas of concern as\nrecommended by the Commission and take appropriate actions in the\ncourse of implementing the reform measures at the DND and AFP.\n\nEstablish a grievance mechanism for AFP personnel to conduct,\ninvestigate, verify, evaluate, recommend and monitor the courses of\naction taken, subject to existing laws, rules and regulations.\nPursue a continuous organizational development process towards the\neradication of graft and corruption in the military establishment.\nExercise such duties and functions as the President deems necessary\nto implement the recommendations contained in the Report of the\nFeliciano Commission dated 17 October 2003."}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Assistance and Cooperation. All departments, agencies of\nthe government, including government-owned or controlled corporations are hereby\ndirected to actively cooperate with and assist in the efficient implementation of this\nExecutive Order. For this purpose, the Presidential Adviser may call upon heads of\nsuch government agencies for such assistance as may, from time to time, be"}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Funding. Funds for the initial operating expenses of the Office\nof the Presidential Adviser to implement the recommendations of the Feliciano\nCommission shall be sourced from the Contingent Fund. Thereafter, funding\nrequirements shall be included in the budget of the Office of the President."}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"Implementation. This Office shall promulgate the\nnecessary implementing rules and regulations as may be necessary to carry out the\nprovisions of this Executive Order."}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 6"},"text":{"en":"Repeal. All orders, rules, regulations and issuances or parts\nthereof which are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H18885-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 7"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of December in the year of Our\nLord, two thousand and three.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE010046\nPOMA Hologram , 23187"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18886"] = {"id":"PH-H18886","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DATED DECEMBER 3, 1936, ESTABLISHING A CLASSIFICATION OF PORTS.","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES DATED DECEMBER 3, 1936, ESTABLISHING A CLASSIFICATION OF PORTS."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_1949.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_1949.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18886-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"3176\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nand Executive Order No. 289, dated July 8, 1940, is\nhereby further amended accordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 19th day of August, in\nthe year of Our Iord, nineteen hundred and forty-nine,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the fourth.\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President\nTEODORO EVANGELISTA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18887"] = {"id":"PH-H18887","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_256_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Classifying Municipal Districts in the Philippines","orig":"Classifying Municipal Districts in the Philippines"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-07-05","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18887-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 256, July 05, 1957 ]\nCLASSIFYING MUNICIPAL DISTRICTS IN THE PHILIPPINES\nPursuant to the provisions of section twenty-six hundred and thirty of the Revised Administrative Code, as\namended by section one of Republic Act Numbered Fifteen hundred and fifteen, the following municip\ndistricts are hereby classified, as herein indicated, in accordance with the schedule provided in said section\none of Republic Act Numbered Fifteen hundred and fifteen, the basis of their average annual revenues for the\nfour fiscal years Nineteen hundred and fifty-two to Nineteen hundred and fifty-five, as certified by the\nGeneral Auditing Office:\nMunicipal District\nMunicipal District\nPangantecan\nGregorio del Pilar\nBacolod Grande\nDitsaan Ramian\nWatu (Balindog)\nMOUNTAIN PROVINCE\nMunicipal Districts Central\nCagayan de Sulu\nSouth Ubian\nPangutaran\nThis classification takes effect as of July 1, 1956.\nThis supersedes Executive Order No. 235, dated February 13, 1957.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of July, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-seven,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines the twelfth.\n(Sgd.) CARLOS P. GARCIA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) FORTUNATO DE LEON\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18888"] = {"id":"PH-H18888","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_256_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Amending Executive Order No. 205 Creating the Foreign Trade","orig":"Amending Executive Order No. 205 Creating the Foreign Trade"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-08-25","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18888-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 256, August 25, 1970 ]\nAMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 242, DATED JUNE 29, 1970, WHICH CREATED THE\nCOOPERATIVES COORDINATING COMMITTEE\nExecutive Order No. 242, dated June 29, 1970, is hereby amended by including Mr. Bartolome Q. Espino,\nRegional Director, Agricultural Productivity Commission, as member of the Cooperatives Coordinating\nCommittee created therein.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 25th day of August, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and seventy.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18889"] = {"id":"PH-H18889","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"P M S LIBRARY MALACANANG &XECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"P M S LIBRARY MALACANANG &XECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18889-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"subsistence\nT\\venty Pesos\nrequirements;\nCOR~ZON C. AQUINO, President\nPlrilippines)\nThe subsistence\nof uatients\nand dispensaries\nof. 1:he P:..!A, P_I\\.FFS and PNP.I\\. shall\nThe subsistence\nINPpersonnel\nundergoing\ninstitutions\nbe incorporated\n-~ppropriations\n-2\n,.-\n4.\nNational.Polite\ncomrriissio.n,\nrespec~i\\-ely,\nimplementing\ninstructions\nand proper~to\n..\nand regulations\nExecu-tr;:r,ire Order\naccordingly.\n,\non .Januaryl,\n1988.\nand eighty-seven.\n~\nBy the President"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18890"] = {"id":"PH-H18890","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"1987, BY RATIONALIZING THE FEES AND CHARGES ON FIREARMS, AMMUNITION, SPARE PARTS, ACCESSORIES, COMPONENTS, EXPLOSIVES, INGREDIENTS, PYROTECHNICS AND FIRECRACKERS","orig":"1987, BY RATIONALIZING THE FEES AND CHARGES ON FIREARMS, AMMUNITION, SPARE PARTS, ACCESSORIES, COMPONENTS, EXPLOSIVES, INGREDIENTS, PYROTECHNICS AND FIRECRACKERS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18890-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The rates of license/registration/permit fees, other charges\nand penal/administrative\nfines relative to firearms, ammunition,\nspare parts,accessorie\ncomponents, explosives, explosive ingredients, pyrotechnics, and\nfirecrackers shall be as follows:\nA. FIREARMS, AMMUNITION, SPARE PARTS, ACCESSORIES AND\nCOMPONENTS:\n1\nAnnual Firearm License Fees\n150.00\n175.00\n200.00\nAir Pistol/Rifle\nRifle Cal. 22 or lower\nPistol/Revolver\nCal. 22 (Ordinary)\nPistol/Revolver\nPLEASE CITE:\n300.00\n~\n\n2/\nPistol/Revolver Cal.357; 41; .44; .45; and\nMagnum Cal.22 Centerfire'\nHigh-Powered Rifle/Sub-machine Gun\n350.00\n500.00\nAny extra slide/barrel or conversion kit shall be assessed\na corresponding license fee amounting to fifty (50) percent\nof the rate for said caliber.\nGovernment employees, whose basic monthly salaries as\nreflected in their latest pay slips do not exceed P5,OOO\nand retirees, whose monthly pensions do not exceed the\nsame amount based on their latest pension slips, shall\npay a firearm license fee of P150 only, regardless of\nthe caliber of the firearm licensed to them.\nThe cost of the license card is not included in the license fee\nbeing paid annually and must be shouldered by the licensee.\n2. Registration Fee\n800.00\na) Reloading Machine\nb) Bullet Proof Vest and Vestments\nThe above amounts are one-time registration fees imposable\nand payable for items registered pursuant to this Executive Order.\n3.\nPermit Fee to Import Firearms, Ammunition, Spare Parts, Accessories,\nand Components for commercial purposes.\nP10.00 per firearm\narrival in the\nPhilippines\nb) Ammunition\nc) Components\nd) Spare Parts -Barrels/Frames/Slides\ne) Reloading\nMachine and its accessories\n\\\\\"\\\n1,000.00\n\n~\n3/\nf) Bullet-proof Vests and Vestments\n500.00\n4.\nStorage Fee (Monthly)\n5.\nPermit Fee to Transport Firearms I Ammunition (Monthly)\na) Gun Club (Quarterly)\n.\nb) Hunting Permit (Quarterly)\nc) Security Agencies\nd) Repair or change of residence\n6.\nRecords Authentication\n7.\nPermit Fee to Carry Firearm Outside of Residence\n8. Permit Fee to Hold Competition\na) Invitational\n2,000.00\nNo fee shall be imposed, however, on PNSA -sponsored!\naccredited competitions.\n9~ Permit Fee for Authority to Di~play Firearms (Annual) P 1,000.00 per\n10. Administrative Fines for Loss of Firearms covered by\nSpecial Permit (SP) or Certificate of Registration (CR)\nShotgun (All Gauges)\n700.00\nPistol! Revolver Cal.22 (Ordinary)\n800.00\nPistol! Revolver Cal.25; .32; .38; .380; 9mm;\n7.65; 6.35 and Magnum Cal.22 Rimfire\n900.00\nPistol! Revolver Cal.357; .41; .45; and Magnum\nCal.22 Centerfire\n1,000.00\nHigh-Powered Rifle ! Sub-M~chine Gun\n1,000.00\n\n4/\n\"\n11. The firearm bond for firearms covered by Regular License (RL) in the\namount equivalent to the following administrative fines shall be deposited as a\ncash bond with any duly designated bank(s) with extensive n~twork in the country\ncapable of servicing the licensed firearms holders nationwide. The corresponding\nbond certificate shall be surrendered by the applicant/licensee to the Firearms and\nExplosives Office, which shall be forfeited in favor of the Philippine National Police\nif and when a particular firearm is reported lost and/or the license is revoked.\n700.00\n800.00\n900.00\n1,000.00\n1,000.00\nb) Shotgun (Alii Gauges)\nRevolver Cal.22 (Ordinary)\nRevolver Cal.25; ,32; .38; .380; 9mm;\n7.65; 6.35; and Magnum Cal. 22 Rimfire\nRevolv~r Cal.357;\nMagnum Cal.22 Centerfire\nHigh-Powered\nSub-Machine\n\"\n12. Seminar Fee for Gun Safety and Responsibility\nB. i:::XPLOSIVES\nAND EXPLOSIVE\nINGREDIENTS:\n1\nPermit Fee to Unload\na) Explosives I Explosive Ingredients in solid form\nb) Explosives I Explosive\nIngredients in liquid form\nc) Detonating cords, safety fuses\nd) Blasting caps, connector\n2. Permit Fee to ImpC'rt Explosives I Explosives Ingredients\n(per application)\n3. Permit Fee to Purchase Explosives / Explosives Ingredients\n(per applicatic n)\n4. Permit Fee to Transport Pyrotechnics I Firecrackers\n(per application)"}},{"id":"PH-H18890-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"The Pr,ilippine National Police is hereby authorized to impose the\nfollowing fees for licenses, issued in connection with the manufacture, importation\nand saie of firearms, ammunition, explosives, explosive ingredients, pyrotechnics\n\"\n~\n\n5/\nand fi~crackers.\nas well as the licenses of indentors, firearm repair shops,\nforemen, and purchasers of explosives and explosive ingredients:\nAMMUNITION.\nACCESSORIES\n~ COMPONENTS:\nLicense (Annual)\n1\nDealer's License\nLicense authorizing the conduct of general business\nsuch as importation, purchase, possession, sale and\ntransfer of firearms, ammunition, spare parts,\naccessories and components. This includes the\nAir Gun Dealer's License (no. 7).\n2.\nManufacturer's License\n10,000.00\nLicense authorizing the conduct of general business\nsuch as. manufacture of firearms, ammunition (Ioadl\nretoad), spare pa~s, accessories and components.\nThis includes the Air Gun Manufacturer's License\n3.\nIndentor's License\n2,000.00\nLicense authorizing the indent of firearms, ammunition\nspare parts, accessories and components.\n4. License to Repair Firearms\n2,000.00\nlicense authorizing the conduct of repair of firearms.\n5.\nRepairman's License\n500.00\n6.\nRecvgnition of Gun Club\nA one-time accreditation fee of a duly registered and\nrecognized gun club. On each succeeding year, the\nduly recognized gun club will renew recognition by\nsubmitting\nthe list of its members and shall pay the\ncorresponding\nfee of P100.00 per member in good\n~\n7. Air Gun Dealer's License\n1,500.00\nLicense authorizing\nthe conduct of general business,\nsuch as importation, purchase. possession. sale and\n\ntransfer of airguns.\n3,000.00\n8. Air Gun Manufacturer's License\nLicense authorizing the conduct of general business,\nsuch as the manufacture of air guns, spare parts,\naccessories and components.\n..\n9.\nLicense to Deal in Spare Parts, Accesories and\n~\nComponents\n1,500.00\nLicense authorizing the conduct of general business,\nsuch as importation, sale and transfer of spare parts,\naccessories and components excluding barrels, slides,\nand frames which are already covered by the Dealer's\n2,500.00\n10.\nAccreditation\nof Firing Range\n1,000.00\ninitial fee\nevery renewal\nFiring ranges owned by the government shall be exempt\nfrom the payment of this accreditation fee.\nEXPLOSIVES AND EXPLOSIVE INGREDIENTS:\n1.\nDealer's License\nUc,cense authorizing the importation, purchase,\npossession, sale, transfer, and general conduct of\nbusiness handling gunpowder, dynamite, explosives\nor their ingredients.\n10,000.00\n2. Manufacturer's\nLicense authorizing\nthe manufacture\nof gunpowder t\nexplosives\nor their ingredients.\n1,000.00\na) Commercial: initial fee\nevery renewal\n'\"\n\"1\n3. Purchaser's License\nLicense authorizing the purchase and possession of\ndynamite, explosives or their ingredients for use of\nmines. quarries. road construction. wrecking or for\n\n7/\nuse in any other legal and lawful occupation.\n500.00\n4.\nForeman's I Blaster's License\nLicense authorizing the purchase and possession of\ndynamite, explQsives or their ingredients by workmen\nin mines, quarries, road construction, wrecking or .\nfor use in any other legal and lawful public or\nprivate work. Licensee must be a qualified blaster\nor must be technically qualified to handle explosives.\nC. PYROTECHNICS AND FIRECRACKERS:\n1\nManufacturer's License\nLicense authorizing the manufacture of pyrotechnics\nand firecrackers.\n500.00\n2. Dealer's License\nLicense authorizing\nthe purchase,\npossession,\ntransfer I and general conduct of business involving\nfirecrackers\nand pyrotechnics."}},{"id":"PH-H18890-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"The Firearms and Explosives Office shall retain twenty percent\n(20%) of the total collections for firearms and explosives fees and charges to fund\nthe direct operational expenses of the FEO other than what is provided for in the\nGeneral Appropriations Act.\nThe Philippine National Police (PNP), Armed Forces of the\nPhilippines (AFP) , and the National Bureau of Investigation (NBI) and other law\nenforcement agencies, shall be exempted from paying the firearm license fees\nprovided for in this Order. Ail other government agencies and instrumentalities\nwhich, by the nature of their jobs, are considered to be revenue-earning entities\nshall pay the necessary firearm license fees and administrative fines provided\nhelein for the firearms used by them in performing functions/duties inherent in the\nmission and organization of the agencies concerned."}},{"id":"PH-H18890-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Private Security Agencies (PASs) and Company Guard Forces\n(CGFs) shall be allowed to pay the cash bond for their existing firearms on a\nstaggered basis over a period of five (5) years from the date of the effectivity of\nthis Order, provided, however, that such payments to be made shall be in equal\namounts each year and provided further that upon the effectivity of this Order,\nPrivate Security Agencies and Company Guard Forces, purchasing or acquiring\nnew firearms shall pay the corresponding cash bond in a maximum of four (4)\ninstallments over a period of one (1) year.\n-.\n\n8/\n6.\nThe Office of the President may issue exemptions from the\npayment of the fee for the issuance of permits to carry firearm outside residence\n(PTFCOR) under such rules or guidelines as it may promulgate.\n\"\n7.\nNo firearm application\nshall be approved\na cer1ificate of attendance\nby the applicant\nin a seminar\nsafety J responsibility\nJ laws, regulations\nand other pertir~ent topics.\nPhilippine\nPolice (PNP), shall promulgate\nrules and regulations\npertaining\nto the implementation\nof this Executive\nsubject to the approval of the Office of the President."}},{"id":"PH-H18890-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 9"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect on January 1, 1996 after\nits publication in at least two (2) newspapers of general circulation.\nThe rates and\ncharges provided under this Executive Order shall be subject to periodic review to\nreflect any changes in the cost of operations, consumer prices and technology.\n~"}},{"id":"PH-H18890-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 10"},"text":{"en":"All orders, issuances, rules and regulations or parts thereof\ninconsistent\nor modified\naccordingly.\nin the year of\nDone in the City of Manila,\nOur Lord, nineteen hundred and ninety five.\n!"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18891"] = {"id":"PH-H18891","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG, M.A.NILA BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. ~~","orig":"MALACANANG, M.A.NILA BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. ~~"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18891-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"1.\nof GFSfv1E that will\neventually\nintegrated/consolidated\nwith SBGFC shall consists of its personnel and all the\nas reflected\nin the 1999 Audited\nincluding subsequent additions/accruals\nthereto. All liabilities which have accrued\nprior to the integration/consolidation\nwith SBGFC shall be honored under the new\n2.\nAll systems,\nprocedures\nand guidelines\npreviously\napproved for GFSME and officially\nsanctioned by higher authorities\nincluding, but not limited to, the Office of the President, Department of Budget\nand Management, Civil Service Commission,\nand Commission on Audit, shall be\nconsidered authorized under the interim set-up until full consolidation/integration\nwith SBGFC is achieved, after which new systems 'Nill be put in place.\n3.\noperations\nconsolidation/integration\nwith SBGFC shall be governed\nby a Management\nCommittee to be composed of five (5) members, as follows:\nThe DTI Undersecretary\nfor Industry and Investments\ndesignated alternate, as Chairman;\n12.\nThe GFSME Executive Director, as Vice Chairman;\nThe head of SBGFC;\n3.\nTwo (2) other members coming from the private sector who\nshall be appointed by the DTI Secretary and shall hold office at\nthe pleasure of the DTI Secretary.\n4.\nThe Management\nshall meet at least once a month or as often\nas the exigencies\nof the service\n-rhe presence\nof at least four (4)\nshall constitute\nand the vote of a majority\nof the members\nthere being a quorum\nshall be necessary\nfor the adoption\nof any act or\nresolution.\nA Committee Secretary shall likewise be appointed by the DTI Secretary\nwho shall be responsible for the preparation of minutes of the meetings and shall\nperform such other duties as may be required to effect the holding of regular\nManagement Committee meetings.\nThe DTI Secretary is hereby authorized to grant reasonable honoraria/fee\nto the members of the Committee and the Secretary thereof.\n~~~.,~~~;~\n,::~:.~1\n¥\n\\\\11\\\\\\1111\\\\\\111\\\\\\\\111\\\\111\\\\\\111\n'18392\n2\n4.\nThe rv1anagement Committee\nis hereby specifically\napplications/restructuring\nof accounts\nP20 Million Pesos.\napplications/restructuring\nof accounts\nfor less than\nmay however,\nbe approved\nof the DTI Undersecretary\nfor Industry\nand Investments\nor his alternate,\na third member\nto be designated\nby the Management\nits members.\napplications/restructuring\nfor less than P5.0 Million\nmay be approved\nby the GFSME\nthe recommendation\nof the Operations\nTo approve the sale of acquired assets, whether real or movable\nand the rules and regulations that will govern the sale of said assets;\nTo approve changes/amendments\nto the existing guidelines on the\nissuance of guarantee;\nTo approve supplemental\nbudgets and such other changes in the\nregular budgets as may be recommended\nby the GFSME Executive\nto the GFSME operations\nexceeding P5.0 Million;\nTo formulate\nrules and regulation\nto carry out\neffectively the functions and purposes of GFSME.\n5.\nContractual commitments\nof GFSME approved by the\nappropriate Committee shall be signed by the GFSME Executive Director for and\nin behalf of DTI.\n6.\nFurther to E.G. 233, the DTI Secretary is authorized to\nreorganize, streamline and adopt a new staffing pattern to suit the requirements\nof the consolidated GFSME-SBGFC.\nThe DTI Secretary is likewise authorized to\nprovide separation benefits to affected personnel, if any, of both GFSME and\nSBGFC which shall be in addition to all gratuity and benefits to which they are\nentitled to under existing laws.\n~.:~.~'.~.!'-'\\~\n,,'-',~::;:\n~-:..~.. :_-~,\n/\\\\11111\\\\11\\\\1111\\\\\\1111111\\\\\\\\\\111\nPJEE Hologram\n118393\n3\n7.\nAll executive orders, rules and regulations or parts\nthereof inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed or revoked\naccordingly.\n8.\nThis Executive\nOrder shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, Philippines this ~\nday of June in the year\nof our Lord Two Thousand.\nBy the President:\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary\n:.\n.~\n..,\n'\n\",...,,-,\n,.~-,\n..\"\n/1111111111111111111111111111111111\\\n118394\n4"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18892"] = {"id":"PH-H18892","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY DECLARATION ON THE EFFECT OF SPECIAL PATENT NO. 3596 AND ESTABLISHING A MAKATI-TAGUIG BOUNDARY COMMITTEE","orig":"MALACAÑANG PMS LIBRARY DECLARATION ON THE EFFECT OF SPECIAL PATENT NO. 3596 AND ESTABLISHING A MAKATI-TAGUIG BOUNDARY COMMITTEE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 256","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00256_2003.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00256_2003.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18892-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Pursuant to the provisions of law and pending the final\nresolution of the territorial dispute between Taguig and Makati, the tracts of land\nsubject of said territorial dispute shall be deemed situated in the Municipality\nof Taguig or City of Makati, until a final determination is issued in Civil Case\nNo. 63896 pending before the Regional Trial Court of Pasig City, Branch 153 or\nany appeals or other related cases therefrom."}},{"id":"PH-H18892-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"The Department of Interior and Local Government is\ndirected to form a special Makati-Taguig Boundary Committee to conduct non-\nbinding discussions to explore the possibility of arriving at a constructive and\nearly resolution of the boundary dispute and to provide for a forum for dialogue\nbetween the two local government units. Said Committee shall be composed of\nthe following:\nSecretary of Interior and Local Government\nOne (1) representative from the Office of the Mayor of the\nCity of Makati\nOne (1) representative from the Office of the Mayor of the\nMunicipality of Taguig\nOne (1) representative from the Office of the Congressional\nRepresentative of the 1St District, City of Makati\nOne (1) representative from the Office of the Congressional\nRepresentative of the Lone District, Taguig-Pateros\nOne (1) representative from the Office of the Solicitor General\nOne (1) neutral legal expert to be appointed by the President"}},{"id":"PH-H18892-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall not be construed as creating or\ngranting any new rights or privileges, and/or affecting or altering the status quo\nof the tracts of land in dispute, or as interfering with the judicial process. Upon\nfinal resolution of the territorial dispute in the above mentioned case or other\nrelated cases as may be decided by the Judicial Department, the statement of\nthe location of said properties in the Special Patent and in all plans and other\nrelated documents and issuances shall be amended, reconciled and made\nconsistent with the final iudicial determination.\n•"}},{"id":"PH-H18892-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"All orders, issuances, rules and regulation, or parts thereof\nwhich are inconsistent with this Executive Order are hereby repealed or modified."}},{"id":"PH-H18892-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila this8th day of December\nof Our Lord, Two Thousand and Three.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPMS LIBRARY BCODE010047"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18893"] = {"id":"PH-H18893","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_257_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Providing for the Implementing Details for Reorganization Plan No. 77 Relative to the Forest Products Research Institute","orig":"Providing for the Implementing Details for Reorganization Plan No. 77 Relative to the Forest Products Research Institute"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 257","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-07-05","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00257_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00257_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18893-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"The organization, functions, and operation of the Forest Products Research Institute, hereinafter\nreferred to as the “Institute,” shall be in accordance with the provisions of Reorganization Plan No. 77,\nhereinafter referred to as the “Plan,” and these Implementing Details."}},{"id":"PH-H18893-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"The organization of the Institute, as graphically depicted in the following organization chart,\nshall consist of the Forest Products Research Board; the Office of the Director which shall consist of the\nDirector and the Assistant Director; and five divisions, namely: Administrative Services Division, Industrial\nInvestigations Division, Wood Technology Division, Chemical Investigations Division, and Wood\nPreservation Division, with their subordinate sections and Units.\n[Organization Chart - FOREST PRODUCTS RESEARCH INSTITUTE]\nFUNCTIONAL STATEMENTS OF THE FOREST PRODUCTS RESEARCH INSTITUTE\nFunctions of the Forest Products Research Board"}},{"id":"PH-H18893-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"The functions, powers, duties, and responsibilities of the Board shall consist of, but not be\nlimited to, those specifically enumerated under section 13 of the Plan.\nFunctions of the Institute"}},{"id":"PH-H18893-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"In addition to the functions, powers, duties, and responsibilities of the Institute as specifically\nenumerated under section 4 of the Plan, it shall have those functions which are transferred to it from the Forest\nProducts Laboratory and Forest Products Research Section, Forest investigation Division of the Bureau of\nForestry which can be interpreted to include, but not be limited to, the following:\na. study, compare, and determine the strength properties and characteristics of different species of wood for\nthe purpose of determining their usefulness as raw materials;\nb. develop new industries or improve old ones so that wood may carry its full share in the industrialization, of\nthe country;\nc. make wood products serve the users better through increased durability and suitability;\nd. conduct studies to distinguish one wood from another and analyze their structural characteristics;\ne. study the best methods of producing plywood and glued products and find the suitability of the different\nspecies for the manufacture of pulp, paper, wallboard, and similar products;\n\nf. conduct natural and artificial seasoning of the different species of wood for industrial use;\ng. study the uses of minor products of the forest, such as rattan, resin, extractives, and others with a view to\ndevelop or improve industries based on them;\nh. study the durability and treatability of different Philippine woods and search for preservatives and methods\nof treatment that will protect them from fungus and insect pests; and\ni. effectuate such other investigations as will make research a sustaining element in the general objectives of\npromoting the integration of forest industries."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H18894"] = {"id":"PH-H18894","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_257_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating National and Local Beautification and Cleanliness Committee to Undertake a Nationwide Beautification and Cleanliness Campaign.","orig":"Creating National and Local Beautification and Cleanliness Committee to Undertake a Nationwide Beautification and Cleanliness Campaign."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 257","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-09-14","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00257_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00257_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H18894-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 257, September 14, 1970 ]\nCREATING NATIONAL AND LOCAL BEAUTIFICATION AND CLEANLINESS COMMITTEE TO\nUNDERTAKE A NATIONWIDE BEAUTIFICATION AND CLEANLINESS CAMPAIGN\nWHEREAS, beauty and cleanliness are basic ideals of all homes, communities and nations; and\nWHEREAS, there is need to reawaken and strengthen the sense of beauty and cleanliness among Filipinos and\nto establish a national organization to pursue this goal;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers\nvested in me by law, do hereby create a National Beautification and Cleanliness Committee to undertake a\nnationwide beautification and cleanliness campaign.\nThe National Committee shall be composed of the following:\nMr. Teodoro F. Valencia\nAny one of the incumbent Presidents of the Rotary Club, the Lions Club, or the Jaycees\nVice-Chairman\nThe Secretary of the PACD\nThe Secretary of Social Welfare\nThe Secretary of Health\nThe Secretary of Education\nThe Secretary of Public Works and Communications\nThe Secretary of Agriculture and Natural Resources\nThe Secretary of National Defense\nDr. Estefania Aldaba-Lim\nMalacañang Liaison\n(To be appointed by the Chairman)\nExecutive Secretary\nThere shall also be created a committee in each province, city, municipality and barrio composed of the\nProvincial/City Committee\nThe Lady of the Governor/Mayor\nRepresentatives from government, civic and religious sectors\nOther officers and members\nMunicipal Committee\nThe Lady of the Mayor\nRepresentatives from government, civic and religious sectors\nOther officers and members\nBarrio Committee\nThe Lady of the Barrio Captain\nLadies of the Barrio Council Officials\nOther officers and members\nThe National Committee and the Local Committees are empowered to call on any government office,\ndepartment, bureau, agency or instrumentality for such assistance as they may need to carry out their\nProclamation No. 20 dated January 13, 1947, Proclamation No. 217 dated November 3, 1950, Proclamation\nNo. 187 dated November 19, 1963, Executive Order No. 32 dated July 12, 1966, and all other proclamations,\nexecutive orders or administrative orders inconsistent herewith are hereby repealed and/or amended\naccordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 14th day of September in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and seventy.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
