  FT["PH-H19007"] = {"id":"PH-H19007","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO.","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EXECUTIVE ORDER NO."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 273","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00273_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00273_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19007-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"by vii-tile of the powers vested in me by law. do hereby approve\nand adopt the \"Phi'ippine\nPlan for Gender-Responsive\nDevelopment.\n1995-\n2025.\" hereinafter referred to as the Plan. and order that:\n1\ngovernment\ndepartments,\ninstrumentalities,\ngovernment-owned\nand -controlled\ncorporations,\nat the national,\nsub-national\nand local levels, are\n1.1\nTo take appropriate\nsteps to ensure the full implementation\nof the policies/strategies\nand programs/projects\n1.2\nTo institutionalize\nGender and Development (GAD) efforts in\ngovernment\nby incorporating\nGAD concerns, as spelled out\nin the Pla,n, in their planning,\nprogramming\nand budgeting\nprocessesj but more specifically to:\nIN REPLYING, PLEASE CITE:\n2\nInclude/incorporate\nGAD concerns in the:\nformulation,\nassessment\nand updating\nannual agency plans:\nb) formulation,\nassessment\nand updating\nto the medium/long-term\ndevelopment\npreparation\nperformance\nassessment\ninvestment plans and other similar documents.\nIncorporate and reflect GAD concerns in their:\nperformance\ncommitment\nindicating\nkey result areas for GAD as well as in\nperformance\nPresident; and\nagency budget proposals\nand work and\nfmancial plans.\n2.\nCommission\nof Filipino\n(NCRFW) , in coordination\nDevelopment Authority\n2.1\nin;lplementation\ngovernment ageQcies; and\n2.2\nCo.nduct the periodic assessment and updating\nevery six years or upon every change in national leadership.\nIn pursuance\nof the foregoing,\nLhe NCRFW may call upon the\nassistance\nof any government\nagency or instrumentality,\ngovernment-owned\nand -controlled\ncorporations\nas well as existing\ninter-agency structures,\nas may be necessary. Non-governmental\norganizations\nand private entities are urged to assist and support\nthe implementation,\nmonitoring,\nassessment and updating of the Plan.\n3.\nThe NCRFW is hereby\nauthorized,\nin consultation\nPresident and concerned government agencies, to issue orders,\nguidelines,\nimplementation,\ncoordination,\nmonitoring,\nassessment\nof the Plan, as well as in the implementation\nprovisions\nFor these purposes,\nNCRFW may constitute\nappropriate\ninter-agency committees.\n3\n4.\nIn view of the Plan's long-term\ngoal of fully\nintegrating\nconcerns into the whole development process, the mainstreaming\nof GAD in various government agencies shall be the responsibility\nof the heads of concerned agencies and their respective offices,\nwith the assistance of their Women in Development\nFocal Points, if any, to ensure institutionalization\n5.\nThe initial\namount necessary for the implementation\nthe appropriations\nof government\nauthorized\nto be set aside\nfor the purpose\n7845,\nbilateral/multilateral\nagencies/organizations\nor those from the\ndevelopment\nassistance (ODA) pursuant\nto Republic\nNo. 7192. Thereafter, budgetary requirements\nfor the succeeding\nyears shall be incorporated\nin General Appropriations\nsubmitted to Congress.\n6.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila. this\n8th day of September\nof Our Lord. Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Five.\nBy the President:\nLEONARDO A. gUISUMBING\nSenior Deputy Executive Secretary\nOfficer- In-Charge, OES\n,.\n2 8 '995\n--~\n\\\\"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19008"] = {"id":"PH-H19008","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":12,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANq PMS LIBRARY INSTITUTIONALIZING THE SYSTEM OF NATIONAL COORDINATION, ASSESSMENT, PLANNING A1~D MONITORING OF THE ENTIRE EDUCATIONAL SYSTEM","orig":"MALACANANq PMS LIBRARY INSTITUTIONALIZING THE SYSTEM OF NATIONAL COORDINATION, ASSESSMENT, PLANNING A1~D MONITORING OF THE ENTIRE EDUCATIONAL SYSTEM"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 273","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 12 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00273_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00273_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19008-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Partjcjpation\nof other Sectors. As the need arises, the Council may\ninvite as resource persons the Secretaries of NED A, DBM, DOST and DOLE as well \" as\nthe participation of representatives from the education, business and other sectors, both\npublic and private and non-governmental organizations, which have direct stakes in\neducation to ensure broad-based consultations and proper dissemination of information\nand advocacy.\nS:EC. 3. Mandates and Functions. -The\nCouncil shall discharge\nresponsibilities in acc.ordance with the following specific mandates:\nto serve as the regular forum for trans-subsectoral consultations on\ncross-cutting policies and programs;\nto harnlonize goals and objectives for the entire education system and\nto dovetail them to national development plans;\n.\nto review existing and proposed programs and projects for tighter\ninter-subsector coordination;\n.\nset priorities\nfor the education\ncorresponding financial requirements;\nto pursue and monitor implementation of the refonns proposed by the\nPresidential Commission on Educational Reform (PCER);\n0\nto establish, overse.e and monitor the implementation of the National\nEducational Evaluation and Testing System (NEETS) and its\noperations;\n.\n{~~\n\n3\nto designate and provide guidelines for Philippine representatives in\ninternational and national conferences/meetings with cross-cutting\nthemes or concerns in education; and\n.\nto convene a biennial National Congress on Education for the purpose\nof assessing, updating/upgr~ding and strengthening of the educatioDal\nsystem and its components.\n.\n,,~"}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"It shall be assisted by a small high-powered Secretariat whose main\nresponsibility is to ensure the efficiency and effectiveness of the NCCE. It shall be\ncomposed of a Director, a permanent staff of five (5) and o$ers seconded to the Council\nas needed from the three (3) member agencies."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"In the discharge of its functions and responsibilities, the NCCE may\ncommission highly-qualified experts/specialists and/or education consultancy groups to\np~ovide specified services."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"It shall adopt its own internal operating rules and procedures and define\nthe duties and responsibilities of the Secretariat, its staffing pattern, and compensation~ched"}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 7"},"text":{"en":"The NCCE shall submit an annual performance report to the Presiden4\nas well as program and policy recommendations affecting the entire education system."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 8"},"text":{"en":"In no case whatsoever shall the NCCE detract from the autonomy and\nindependence ofDECS, TESDA and CHED.,"}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 9"},"text":{"en":"Statistics for Educational Planning -For the purpose of carrying out\nthe mandates of the NCCE, the National Statistics Office (NSO) is hereby directed to\nstrengthen its core or basic unit responsible for the generation and analysis of education\nand training statistics and to systematize its operational links with the st':ltistical units in\nthe Department of Education, Culture and Sports, Commission on Higher Education and\nTechnical Education and Skills Development Authority.\nThe NCCE shall coordinate\nwith the NSO in all matters pertaining to the generation, analysis, utilization\ndissemination of all educational statistics and infonnation."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 10"},"text":{"en":"Government agencies are hereby directed to second and/or detail\ncompetent individuals to the NCCE as may be requested.\nIrfifl1\\;I~;IIIIIIII!!I!!!I!!I!III!I!!IIIII!I!EE\n'19303"}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 11"},"text":{"en":"The Council is directed to convene the first National Congress on the\nState of Philippine Education by 200 I in order to, among others, monitor the fulfillment\nof all the policy and program recommendations of both the EDCOM and the PCER. ."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 12"},"text":{"en":"Initial Funding of the NCCE. -The sum of fourteen million pesos is\nhereby appropriated from the President's Social Fund for the initial mobilization and fIrSt\nyear of operation of the NCCE.\nThereafter, the sum of Ten Million Pesos\n(pIO,OOO,OOO.OO)\nshall be included in the General Appropriations Act."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 13"},"text":{"en":"Repealing Clause. -All\nexecutive issuances inconsistent with this\nExecutive Order are hereby repealed or amended accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H19008-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 14"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity. -This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this ,~\nLord, two thousand.\n, in the year of Our\n-\n.~\n(:~=:::::;7/'-\nFfv1S lIB~~ARY\n,\nBy the President:\n---~~\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19009"] = {"id":"PH-H19009","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARV BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE OPERATION OF THE GOVERNMENT'S DRUG TREATMENT AND REHABILITATION CENTERS AND PROGRAM NATIONWIDE TO THE DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH","orig":"MALACANANG PMS LIBRARV BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES TRANSFERRING THE OPERATION OF THE GOVERNMENT'S DRUG TREATMENT AND REHABILITATION CENTERS AND PROGRAM NATIONWIDE TO THE DEPARTMENT OF HEALTH"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 273","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00273_2004.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00273_2004.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19009-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Transfer of PNP and NBI Treatment and\nRehabilitation Centers to DOH - The existing government drug treatment\nand rehabilitation centers (TRC's), including the PNP TRCs in Bicutan, Iloilo,\nAlbay, Cebu and BI TRCs in Tagaytay, Cagayan de Oro and Cebu, along with\nthe corresponding logistics (Maintenance Operating and Other Expenses,\nPersonnel Services and equipment) are hereby transferred to the DOH.\nTransition Committee - A Transition Committee shall be\ncreated to assist the DOH in implementing this Order. The Committee shall be\ncomposed of the DO as Chair and the following as members; Department of\nInterior and Local Government, Department of Justice, Department of Budget\nand Management and the Private Sector Representative of the Dangerous Drugs\nThe Transition Committee shall ensure among others, the actual resource\ntransfer from PP and NBI to the DOH, including newly constructed buildings.\nThe Committee shall ensure that no personnel shall be displaced, nor shall there\nbe diminution of their salaries and benefits, and that affected personnel shall be\ngiven the option to stay with their mother units. The Committee shall ensure the\nsmooth turn-over/transition of administration and control of the above identified\nareas to the DOH.\nFunding - An initial amount of P350 Million from the P 1\nBillion standby fund for Anti-Dangerous Drugs Campaign shall be allotted to the\nDOH for it to immediately assume the mandate to operate existing government\nTRCs in 2004 and improve treatment and rehabilitation programs. The current\nallotment for TRCs operated and maintained by the PP and BI shall be\ntransferred to the DOH in the General Appropriations Act (GAA) FY 2005. The\nDepartment of Budget and Management shall help identify the specific allotments\nwhich include Personnel Salaries and Maintenance, Operating and Other\nPOMA Hologram • 23892\n\nThe Department of Budget and Management shall provide for an\nadditional P 300 Million to be included in the GAA FY 2005 for the DOH to hire\nadditional personnel, train/improve capability of existing personnel,\nmodernize/expand existing facilities and establish more TRCs specially in regions\nwhere there are none.\nSeparability Clause - In the event that any provision\nhereof is declared invalid by any competent court or tribunal, the other\nprovisions hereof shall remain unaffected, and shall remain in full force and\nimmediately.\nEffectivity - This Executive Order shall take effect\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this 20TH day of Jan in the year of Our\nLord Two Thousand and Four.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPOMA Hologram * 23893"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19010"] = {"id":"PH-H19010","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_274_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating the Municipality of Olutanga in the Province of Zamboanga Del Sur","orig":"Creating the Municipality of Olutanga in the Province of Zamboanga Del Sur"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-10-16","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19010-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 274, October 16, 1957 ]\nCREATING THE MUNICIPALITY OF OLUTANGA IN THE PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA DEL SUR\nPursuant to the provisions of section sixty-eight of the Revised Administrative Code, the islands of Olutanga,\nLampinigan, Lutangan, and Talata, composing of the barrios and sitios of Suba Nipa, Talusan, Sagasa,\nLeparot, Plasiris, Cabato-an, Bangalan, Calais, Cawilan, Gandaan, Tambanan, Bontalian, Pinaling, Taguisian,\nTando Comot, Culiran, Olutanga, Port Sibulan, Calabasa, and Tawitawi, all of the municipality of Alicia,\nprovince of Zamboanga del Sur, are hereby segregated from said municipality and organized into an\nindependent municipality in said province, to be known as the municipality of Olutanga with the seat of\ngovernment at the barrio of Suba Nipa.\nThe boundary between the municipality of Alicia and the municipality of Olutanga shall be the middle of the\nchannel or strait which separates the barrios, sitios, and islands above-named from the rest of the territory of\nAlicia on the mainland.\nThe municipality of Alicia shall have the same territory-minus that comprised in the municipality of Olutanga.\nThe municipality of Olutanga shall begin to exist after November 12, 1957, upon the appointment and\nqualification of the mayor, vice-mayor, and a majority of the councilors thereof and upon the certification by\nthe Secretary of Finance that said municipality is financially capable of implementing the provisions of the\nMinimum Wage Law and providing for all the statutory obligations and ordinary essential services of a\nregular municipality and that the mother municipality of Alicia, after the segregation therefrom of the territory\ncomprised in the municipality of Olutanga, can still maintain creditably its municipal government, meet all its\nstatutory and contractual obligations, and provide for the essential municipal services.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 16th day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nfifty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the twelfth.\n(Sgd.) CARLOS P. GARCIA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) FORTUNATO DE LEON\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19011"] = {"id":"PH-H19011","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_274_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Requiring the Submission of An Annual Program of Procurement By the Departments, Bureaus, Offices and Agencies of the National Government.","orig":"Requiring the Submission of An Annual Program of Procurement By the Departments, Bureaus, Offices and Agencies of the National Government."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-11-24","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19011-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 274, November 24, 1970 ]\nREQUIRING THE SUBMISSION OF AN ANNUAL PROGRAM OF PROCUREMENT BY THE\nDEPARTMENTS, BUREAUS, OFFICES AND AGENCIES OF THE NATIONAL GOVERNMENT\nWHEREAS, the government spends a tremendous amount of money annually for the purchase of supplies,\nmaterials and equipment to meet all government needs;\nWHEREAS, emergency purchases and piecemeal requisitions are found to be wasteful and extravagant and\ntherefore must be done sparingly;\nWHEREAS, it is imperative that procurement of supplies, materials and equipment be handled systematically\nand judiciously in order to obtain the most advantageous terms from the suppliers; and\nWHEREAS, to achieve an economical, efficient and effective procurement system, the using agencies and the\nBureau of Supply Coordination must devise a system of projecting and planning their supply needs to be used\nas a basis for a workable procurement program;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, FERDINAND E.MARCOS, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers\nvested in me by law, do hereby order:\nHeads of departments, bureaus, offices and agencies of the National Government shall submit an Annual\nProcurement Program showing a projection of their procurement needs for a period of one (1) year starting\nJuly 1 and ending June 30 of every fiscal year. This Annual Procurement Program shall include, among other\nthings, a complete description or specification of the items arranged according to commodity groupings, the\nquantity of each kind distributed by quarter and the estimated cost.\nSupplementary Procurement Programs may be submitted in case of increase hi supply requirements to be\nfunded out of additional funds allocated. An Amendatory Procurement Program may also be submitted if\nthere are changes affecting the Annual Procurement Program and/or the Supplementary Procurement\nAll Procurement Programs shall be approved by the department head concerned.\nThe Annual Procurement Program shall be filed with the Bureau of Supply Coordination not later than April 1\nimmediately preceding the ensuing fiscal year covered by the Program.\nThe Amendatory or Supplementary Procurement Programs shall be prepared and submitted any time during\nthe fiscal year as the need arises.\nThe Bureau of Supply Coordination, upon receipt of these plans, shall draw up its own program of\nprocurement. It shall consolidate and categorize the items to find out the overall needs of the Government and\ndetermine the system of procurement that will be most effective, economical and expeditious. It may group\nthese items into the following:\n(1) those that will be placed under the Direct Order and Payment System;\n(2) those that may be procured through the normal bidding procedure by the Bureau of Supply Coordination\nupon submission of the proper requisition;\n(3) those whose procurement may be recommended for delegation to, or requested directly by, the agencies\nconcerned if it is found out that it will be more advantageous for the agencies to procure;\n(4) those that may be recommended for procurement by negotiation under existing regulations including those\nobtainable from government agencies and foreign governments;\n(5) those that may be carried in the stores of the Bureau of Supply Coordination; and\n(6) those that may be filled from surplus or excess items.\nThe Bureau of Supply Coordination’s Consolidated Program of Procurement shall be forwarded to the\nSecretary of General Services for approval. After its approval, the Secretary of General Services shall issue\nthe necessary implementing instructions. The Bureau of Supply Coordination shall advise the departments,\nbureaus, offices and agencies concerned of the action taken on their plans for their information and guidance.\nThe Secretary of General Services shall issue the necessary supplementary rules and regulations to implement\nDone in the City of Manila, this 24th day of November in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and seventy.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19012"] = {"id":"PH-H19012","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAf:ANG ~ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 274 THE PRESIDENTIAL FOR YOUTH AFF\".IRS AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES under Section 13. the 19.87 Constitution recognizes of the youth in nation-building and protect intellectual, in the youth patriotism and nationalism, and encourage involvement government and programs formulation and implementation \\ NOW, THEkEFOHL, CORr.ZON C.'hilippines, do hereby order: There is hereby created the Presidential -for Youth I..ffairs, hereinafter re!~~E_e~_to as the ~ounc_~_~_1-~~~- of the President.- The Council be composed of a Chairman and (4) members to be appointed by the President. '.'. (21) ,- ,- : - (30) years of age.","orig":"MALACAf:ANG ~ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 274 THE PRESIDENTIAL FOR YOUTH AFF\".IRS AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES under Section 13. the 19.87 Constitution recognizes of the youth in nation-building and protect intellectual, in the youth patriotism and nationalism, and encourage involvement government and programs formulation and implementation \\ NOW, THEkEFOHL, CORr.ZON C.'hilippines, do hereby order: There is hereby created the Presidential -for Youth I..ffairs, hereinafter re!~~E_e~_to as the ~ounc_~_~_1-~~~- of the President.- The Council be composed of a Chairman and (4) members to be appointed by the President. '.'. (21) ,- ,- : - (30) years of age."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19012-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"The Council\nmembers must\nbe of good moral\nmust not have been convicted\nmoral turpitude,\nand must have occupied\nof responsibility\nand leadership\nin established\nyouth organizations.\nThe Chairman\nand members shall\nat the pleasure\nof the President\nThe Council\nhave the following\nresponsibilities\nTo recommend to the Office\nof the President,\ndevelopment\nand programs,\nin coordination\nconsultation\nthe youth sector\nand the concerned\ngovernment\ndepartments\nand agencies;\n.\nTo comI!lunicatE:\nand consult\ngovernment\ndepartrne!lt,\nthe specific\nand concern;\na consultative\nmechanism which shall\ncontinuing\nbetween the\ngovernment\nand the youth sector\non the proper\nand evaluation\nof programs and projects\nand studies\nand concernsj\nTo participate\nin international\nyouth participation\nand implement\nforeign-sponsored\nyouth projects,\n~nd assigned\nby the Office\nof the President;\n~;.;~~\nTo facilitate\nand coordinate\nthe implementation\nthe Philippines\nof international\nyouth prograrns~\nand assigned\nby the Office\nof the President;\nlegislation.\nand programs\nof the government\nto the youth,\nin consultation\nand recommend appropriate\nthe assistance\nand recommendRtions\nof anydepartment.\nin the perJrrmance_Qf\nand endorse\nthe organizational\nand staffing\nof the Council\nto the President.\nthe necessary\nadministrative\nand subordinate\nto t~e provisions\nof existing\n~aws andregulations;\ndiscipline\nany employee,\ndisapprove\nof eulployees,\nprovisions\nand regulations;\n(1)\nAr,prove and submit\nto the Office\nof the President,\non the progress\nand accomplishments\nof theCouncil's\nand the annual\nand supplemental\nof theCouncil;\n.\nas may be authorized\nby the President.\nThe President\nthe Council,\nupon the recommendation\nof the Council\nand who sh~ll\nbe ,aQswerable\nto the Council\nmembers, and shall\nthe following\n(a) To implement\nthe policies,\nprograms and decisions\nof the Council;\nTo supervise\nthe operations\nand internal\nthe Council,\ncoordination\nthe Councilmembers;\nto the administrative\nand technical\nof the Council;\nTo maintain\nthe or,sanizational\nof the Council,\ncoordination\nthe Council\nthe Councii\nperformance\nand accomplishments\nof the Council\nand programs,\nas to recommend allocations\nsuch programs;\n'ro recommend\nand supplemental\nconsideration\nand approval\n{o::::) To perform\notherfunctions--as--rnay\nbe authoriz~d\nby the Council.\nThe KabataanG :tSaran;ay l'lational\nunder Executive\n28, 1982,\nthe Ycuth Development\nand the becretaria.t\nare hereby abolishedo\n.\na co!:1mittee to oversee\nand supervise\nthe winding\nup of the Kabataang ~rangay\nSecretariat\nthe disposition\nproperties,\nand equipment.\nThe Committee\nby the Presidential\nYouth Affairs\nbe composecl of the representatives\nthe Department\nof Education,\n(DECS) , theDept.\nand \"Deveiopment (DSWD) , the Dept.\nGovernments\n(DLG) , end the i\"iational\nfiianpower and Youth Council\nappropriations,\nproperties,\nDevelopment\nSecretariat\ntransferred\nthe Council.\nThe functions\nand remaining\nprof,erties,\nPhilipr,ine\nCommission\non International\ntransferred\n-4-\nThe amounts herein\ntransferred\nThereafter,\nbe included\nin the General\nAppropriations\nregulations\ninconsistent\nor modified\naccordingly.\n.SECTION 7.Immediately.\nThis Executive\nOrder shall\nDone in the City\nhundred and eiGhty-seven.\n(SGD.) CORAZON\nof the Philippines\nBy the President\n~\\"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19013"] = {"id":"PH-H19013","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EST ABLISHING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION ON BICOL TOURISM SPECIAL DEVELOPMENT PROJECT","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES EST ABLISHING THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION ON BICOL TOURISM SPECIAL DEVELOPMENT PROJECT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19013-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"The Commission shall be an advisory body to the President and\nshall exercise the following functions and responsibilities:\nArticulate the development goals, objectives, programs and projects\nof the Sical Region Tourism Master Plan;\nCause the update and refinement\nof the Bicol Region Tourism\nMaster Plan within\nthe context of the Medium Term Philippine\nDevelopment\nPlan, Regional Development\nPlan, and the\nDevelopment Plan of the local government units (LGUs);\nCause the conduct of feasibility study, evaluation, and financing of\nthe project components of the BRTMP;\nProvide overall direction,\ncoordination,\nand supervision\nplanning, implementation and monitoring\nof the BRTMP;\nEnlist the support\nand assistance\nfrom government and non-\ngovernment institutions\nin planning and implementing the BRTMP;\nEnter into contracts as may be necessary in the implementation\nthe BRTMP, subject to existing laws, rules and regulations;\nOrganize the Project Management Office. define its organizationalset-up.\nits i staff~ng pattern\nDirector and staff. subject to approval of the Department of Budget\nand Management;\nimplementing\nrules and regulations\npertaining\ninternal operations of the Project Management Office; and\nSubmit to the President quarterly progress reports on the Project\nand such other reports as may be required."}},{"id":"PH-H19013-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"The Commission may call upon any government agency, office\nor bureau for assistance in the discharge of, and form committees to facilitate\nthe performance of, its functions and responsibilities."}},{"id":"PH-H19013-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"The amount of Five Million Pesos (-PS,OOO,OOO.OO),\nfrom funds of the DOT, shall be released for the operations of the Commission\nfor 1995. Appropriations\nfor the succeeding years shall be incorporated in the\nbudget proposals under the Office of the President."}},{"id":"PH-H19013-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"All executive issuances, orders, rules and regulations,\nthereof, inconsistent\nwith this Executive Order are hereby revoked or modifiedaccordins\n\n\\'\n-3 -\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 14th\nyear of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Five.\nBy the President:\n~\nExecutive Secretary\n~~"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19014"] = {"id":"PH-H19014","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALA CAN AN P ALA C~ PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHll..IPPINES","orig":"MALA CAN AN P ALA C~ PMS LIBRARY BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHll..IPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19014-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Section 7 orE.D. 395 is amended as follows:\nTh~ budget of the PCP Secretariat and the PCP Executive Committee (PCP-ExCom)\nfor the year 2000 shall be sourced from the remaining PCP budget for 2000 originally\nallocated for the activities of the PCP Joint Secretariat and Technical Committee.\nrespectively. lodged in the NEDA budget. The NEDA shall release the funds in the form of\ncash advances to NWPC which shall in turn submit to NEDA a duly audited COA report on\nthe utilization of the cash advances.\nHenceforth. the budget for the operations of the Council, Executive Committee and\nSecretariat shall be incorporated in the budget of the NWPC-DOLE.\nHowever, the budget\npreparation and utilization of the PCP funds with respect to the allocation of the Council, the\nPCP-ExCom and the PCP Secretariat shall be determined through a mutual agreement by the\nPDC-DAP and NWPC-DOLE and recommended jointly through the PCP-ExCom to the\nCouncil Chair for approval.\nThe government agencies involved in the implementation of the Medium-Term\nNational Action Agenda for Productivity (MNAAP). 2000-2004 shall continue to include in\ntheir respective budgets the necessary funds required for their productivity programs and\nactivities."}},{"id":"PH-H19014-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE, in the City of Manila, this ~\nin the year of Our Lord, Two\nprv1S liBRARY\nBy the President:\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary\n~~"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19015"] = {"id":"PH-H19015","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REVISE THE COMPOSITION OF THE ELEMENTS OF THE ANTI- SMUGGLING INTELLIGENCE AND INVESTIGATION CENTER","orig":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES REVISE THE COMPOSITION OF THE ELEMENTS OF THE ANTI- SMUGGLING INTELLIGENCE AND INVESTIGATION CENTER"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 274","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 2 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00274_2004.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00274_2004.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19015-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"Section 3 of EO 155, s. 2002, is hereby amended to read as\nthe following:\n\"Sec. 3. Composition - The Center shall be composed of elements of\na. Armed Forces of the Philippines;\nb. Bureau of Customs;\nc. Philippine National Police;\nd. Philippine Coast Guard; and\ne. Department of Justice."}},{"id":"PH-H19015-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity - This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\n\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 26TH day of Jan, in the year of Our\nLord, Two Thousand and Four.\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19016"] = {"id":"PH-H19016","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_275_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipality of Jose Abad Santos, Province of Davao, From the Barrio of Butulan to the Barrio of Caburan, Same Municipality","orig":"Transferring the Seat of Government of the Municipality of Jose Abad Santos, Province of Davao, From the Barrio of Butulan to the Barrio of Caburan, Same Municipality"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-10-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19016-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 275, October 18, 1957 ]\nTRANSFERRING THE SEAT OF GOVERNMENT OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF JOSE ABAD SANTOS,\nPROVINCE OF DAVAO, FROM THE BARRIO OF BUTULAN TO THE BARRIO OF CABURAN, SAME\nMUNICIPALITY\nPursuant to the provisions of section sixty-eight of the Revised Administrative Code, the seat of government\nof the municipality of Jose Abad Santos, province of Davao, is hereby transferred from the barrio of Butulan\nto the barrio of Caburan of said municipality.\nThis accordingly amends Executive Order No. 156, series of 1948.\nThe transfer herein made shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 18th day of October, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nfifty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the twelfth.\n(Sgd.) CARLOS P. GARCIA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) ENRIQUE C. QUEMA\nAssistant Executive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19017"] = {"id":"PH-H19017","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_275_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Modifying the Rates of Import Duty on Certain Imported Articles as Provided Under Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven, Otherwise Known as the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines, as Amended.","orig":"Modifying the Rates of Import Duty on Certain Imported Articles as Provided Under Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven, Otherwise Known as the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines, as Amended."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-11-26","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19017-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"The articles specifically listed hereunder as classified under Section 401 of Republic Act\nNumbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven shall pay the following rates of import duty:\nDescription of Articles Rate of Duty\nRate of Duty\n27.09\nPetroleum and shale oils,crude\n27.10\nPetroleum and shale oils, other than crude; preparations not otherwise provided for, containing not less than\n70 per cent by weight of petroleum or shale oils, these oils “being the basic constituents of the preparations:\nA. Light oils (e.g., petroleum other, gasoline, white spirit)\nB. Medium oils (e.g., kerosene and tractor fuel)\nC. Heavy oils,(lubricating oils, paraffin liquid or white oils)"}},{"id":"PH-H19017-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"After the expiration of thirty (30) days from the issuance of this Order, all the above-described\narticles entered or withdrawn from warehouses, in the Philippines, for consumption shall he subject to the\nrates of import duty herein prescribed."}},{"id":"PH-H19017-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Any unwarranted increase in prices of local products benefited by these tariff changes may he\nsufficient ground for the revocation of such tariff changes.\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\n\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19018"] = {"id":"PH-H19018","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"GR_~DU.\\L AND ORDERLr- Pl\\.R.;~fIT::ITARY THE CIVLLI$...t.' FOR OTHER PURPOSES","orig":"GR_~DU.\\L AND ORDERLr- Pl\\.R.;~fIT::ITARY THE CIVLLI$...t.' FOR OTHER PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19018-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"Bonafide\nauthorized\nparamilitary\nequi-valent\na-v\"ailability\nappropriations\nHome Defense\nSECTION 6\", 'rhe\nof National\npromu.lgate\nrf'cg-u.latjons\n\n2/\n.\n[\n7.\nPre.sidential\n1016,\nand regulations\ninconsistent\nor modified\naccordingly.\ncompletion\na newspaper\ncirculation\nthe Philippines.\n\",\n-,\nand eighty-seven."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19019"] = {"id":"PH-H19019","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING A COMMITTEE FOR THE SPECIAL PROTECTION OF CHILDREN FROM ALL FORMS OF NEGLECT, ABUSE, CRUELTY, EXPLOITATION, DISCRIMINATION AND OTHER CONDITIONS PREJUDICIAL TO THEIR DEVELOPMENT","orig":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING A COMMITTEE FOR THE SPECIAL PROTECTION OF CHILDREN FROM ALL FORMS OF NEGLECT, ABUSE, CRUELTY, EXPLOITATION, DISCRIMINATION AND OTHER CONDITIONS PREJUDICIAL TO THEIR DEVELOPMENT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19019-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"There is hereby created a Special Committee for Children to be\ncomposed of:\n1. The Secretary of Justice\n2. The Secretary of Social Welfare and\nDevelopment\nCo-Chairman\n3. The Chairman of the Commission on\nHuman Rights\n4. Commissioner of the Bureau of Immigration\nA representative with a rank not lower than undersecretary from the following:\n5. Department of Labor and Employment\nDEPLYING, PLEASE CITE:\n1951298\n\n6. Department of Tourism\n7. Department of the Interior and Local\nGovernment\n8. Department of Foreign Affairs\n9. Three representatives of private\norganizations to be nominated\nby said groups and appointed by the"}},{"id":"PH-H19019-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"The Committee shall exercise the following functions and duties:\nTo report to the President actions taken to address specific issues on\nchild abuse and exploitation brought to the Committee's attention.\nTo direct other agencies to immediately respond to the problems brought\nto their attention and to report to the Committee on action taken.\nTo perform such other functions and duties as may be necessary to meet\nthe objectives of the Committee."}},{"id":"PH-H19019-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"The Council for the Welfare of Children shall act as the Secretariat of\nthe Committee."}},{"id":"PH-H19019-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"The initial amount of P10,000,000.00 is hereby authorized to be\nreleased from the Presidential Social Fund."}},{"id":"PH-H19019-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 14thday of September\nLord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Five.\n, in the year of Our\nBy the President:\n(RUBEN D. TORRES\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19020"] = {"id":"PH-H19020","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES SCIENTIFIC COOPERATION FROM THE LIST OF COUNTRIES COVERED BY LETTER OF INSTRUCTIONS","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES SCIENTIFIC COOPERATION FROM THE LIST OF COUNTRIES COVERED BY LETTER OF INSTRUCTIONS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19020-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"with the country's\nnationalinteres\nPhilippine\nInternational\nTra.ding Corporation\nis becoming an unnecessary\nbarrier to trade.\nNOW, THEREFORE,\nI, JOSE,PH EJERCITO\nof the Philippines,\nby virtue of the powers vested in me by law, do hereby\nThe Committee\non Scientific\nand Technical Cooperation with Socialist\nCountries to remove the Socialist Republic of Vietnam from the list of countries\ncovered by Letter of Instructions No. 444.\nin the Year of\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 3{)'t) day of\nOur Lord, Two Thousand.\n/)\n(:==:7-- ~\nprv'iS LIBRARY\n-\n.--,,'~\nBy the President:\n.~-\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19021"] = {"id":"PH-H19021","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES COMMISSIONING JOINTLY THE PHILIPPINE SPORTS COMMISSION AND THE PHILIPPINE SPORTS ASSOCIATION FOR THE DIFFERENTLY-ABLED, INC. (PHILSPADA) TO HOST THE 3RD ASEAN PARAGAMES 2005","orig":"MALACAÑANG BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES COMMISSIONING JOINTLY THE PHILIPPINE SPORTS COMMISSION AND THE PHILIPPINE SPORTS ASSOCIATION FOR THE DIFFERENTLY-ABLED, INC. (PHILSPADA) TO HOST THE 3RD ASEAN PARAGAMES 2005"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 275","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00275_2004.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00275_2004.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19021-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"from donors or income tax to the extent and under the conditions allowed by\nexisting law.\nI call upon the Department of Education, Department of Transportation\nand Communications, Department of National Defense, Department of the\nInterior and Local Government, Department of Social Welfare and Development,\nDepartment of Tourism, Department of Health, Department of Public Works and\nHighways, Department of Foreign Affairs, Philippine Amusement and Gaming\nCorporation, The Philippine Charity Sweepstakes Office, National Council for the\nWelfare of Disabled Persons, Philippine Information Agency and other\ngovernment agencies, as well as the mass media and the entire citizenry, for\ntheir wholehearted support and cooperation on this worthy undertaking.\nFurther, government agencies are authorized to use their respective budget to\nfund the activities for the purpose.\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, I have hereunto set my hand and caused the\nseal of the Republic of the Philippines to be affixed.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 26TH day of Jan\nLord, Two Thousand and Four.\n, in the year of Our\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPOM) Hologram • 24031"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19022"] = {"id":"PH-H19022","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_276_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Amending Executive Order No. 254 Dated June 27, 1957, Entitled Creating the Juan Luna Centennial Commission","orig":"Amending Executive Order No. 254 Dated June 27, 1957, Entitled Creating the Juan Luna Centennial Commission"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-10-31","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19022-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 276, October 31, 1957 ]\nAMENDING EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 254 DATED JUNE 27, 1957, ENTITLED “CREATING THE\nJUAN LUNA CENTENNIAL COMMISSION”\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by law, I, Carlos P. Grarcia, President of the Philippines, do hereby\namend Executive Order No. 254, dated June 27, 1957, by designating Mr. Ramon Campos, Mr. Carlos E. de\nSilva, Dr. Buenaventura J. Rollo, and Mayor Esmeraldo C. Agabin of Badoc, Ilocos Norte, as additional\nmembers of the Juan Luna Centennial Commission created therein.\nDone in the City of Manila, this. 31st day of October, in the year of Our Lord nineteen hundred and\nfifty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the twelfth.\n(Sgd.) CARLOS P. GARCIA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) FORTUNATO DE LEON\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19023"] = {"id":"PH-H19023","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_276_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Modifying the Rates of Import Duty on Certain Imported Articles as Provided Under Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven, Otherwise Known as the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines, as Amended.","orig":"Modifying the Rates of Import Duty on Certain Imported Articles as Provided Under Republic Act Numbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven, Otherwise Known as the Tariff and Customs Code of the Philippines, as Amended."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-11-26","completenessNote":"全文，共 3 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19023-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"The articles specifically listed hereunder as classified under Section 401 of Republic Act\nNumbered Nineteen Hundred Thirty-Seven shall pay the following rates of import duty:\nDescription of Articles\nRate of Duty\n11.01\nCereal Flours:A. Wheat flour1. Flour for glue extender or binder properly colored or denatured to render it\ninedible when imported directly by bonafide plywood manufacturers for their exclusive use in the\nmanufacture of plywood upon certification by the Tariff Commission\n2. Flour for macaroni and spaghetti when imported directly by bonafide macaroni and spaghetti manufacturers\nfor their exclusive use in the manufacture of such products upon certification by the Tariff Commission\n11.07\nMalt,unroosted or roasted but not further processed\n12.06\nHop cones and lupulin\n48.01\n\nPaper and paperboard (including cellulose wadding) machine made:A. Paper:1. x x x x x\n9. Cup converting paper when imported directly by bonafide paper cup manufacturers certified as such by the\nTariff Commission and/or the National Economic Council"}},{"id":"PH-H19023-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"After the expiration of thirty (30) days from the issuance of this Order, all the above-described\narticles entered or withdrawn from warehouses, in the Philippines, for consumption shall be subject to the\nrates of import duty herein prescribed."}},{"id":"PH-H19023-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"Any unwarranted increase in prices of local products benefited by these tariff changes may be\n.sufficient ground for the revocation of such tariff changes.\nDONE IN THE CITY OF MANILA, this 26thday of November in the year of our Lord, nineteen hundred and\n(SGD.) FERDINAND E. MARCOS\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(SGD.) ALEJANDRO MELCHOR\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19024"] = {"id":"PH-H19024","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Revising the Integrated Compensation Scheme for Uniformed Personnel of the Integrated National Police","orig":"Revising the Integrated Compensation Scheme for Uniformed Personnel of the Integrated National Police"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1981-09-10","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_1981_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_1981_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19024-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 1"},"text":{"en":"The following salary schedule shall apply to all uniformed personnel of the Integrated National Police;\nSALARY SCHEDULE\nS A L A R Y S T E P S\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\nPolice/Fire p/a\n3115\n3274\n\n3441\n3616\n3800\n3994\n4198\n4412\nPolice/Fire p/a\n29148\n30636\n32196\n33840\n35568\n37380\n39288\n41292\n2429\n2553\n2683\n2820\n2964\n3115\n3274\n3441\nPolice/Fire p/a\n25116\n26388\n27732\n29148\n30636\n32196\n33840\n35568\n2093\n2199\n2311\n\n2429\n2553\n2683\n2820\n2964\nPolice/Fire p/a\n20580\n21624\n22728\n23892\n25116\n26388\n27732\n29148\n1715\n1802\n1894\n1991\n2093\n2199\n2311\n2329\nPolice/Fire p/a\n16044\n16860\n17724\n18636\n19584\n20580\n21624\n22728\n1337\n1405\n1477\n1553\n\n1632\n1715\n1802\n1994\nPolice/Fire p/a\n13152\n13824\n14532\n15264\n16044\n16860\n17724\n18636\nLieutenant p/m\n1096\n1152\n1211\n1272\n1337\n1405\n1477\n1553\nPolice/Fire p/a\n7992\n8400\n8832\n9288\n9756\n10260\n10776\n11328\nSergeant p/m\n666\n700\n736\n774\n813\n\n855\n898\n944\nPolice/Fire p/a\n7236\n7608\n7992\n8400\n8832\n9288\n9756\n10260\nCorporal p/m\n603\n634\n666\n700\n736\n774\n813\n855\nPatrolman/ Fireman p/a\n6552\n6888\n7236\n7608\n7992\n8400\n8830\n9288\nFirst Class p/m\n546\n574\n603\n634\n666\n700\n\n736\n774\nPatrolman/ p/a\n5928\n6240\n6552\n6888\n7236\n7608\n7992\n8400\n494\n520\n546\n574\n603\n634\n666\n700"}},{"id":"PH-H19024-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"Readjustment of Salary. The salary of a member of the Integrated National Police as prescribed under"}},{"id":"PH-H19024-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"0 of Letter of Implementation No. 98 as adjusted to the rates of Executive Order No. 688 dated\nMarch 19, 1981 shall be readjusted to conform with the rates of preceding Section 1 hereof, subject to the\nfollowing guidelines:\n2.1 In case the salary of any members of the Integrated National Police is lower than the first salary step\nprescribed in Section 1 such salary shall be raised to the rate corresponding to the first salary step prescribed\n2.2 In case the salary of a member of the Integrated National Police is equal or above the first step prescribed\nin Section 1 hereof, the member concerned shall continue to receive the same salary rate.\nSec. 3. The guidelines for the implementation of this Order shall be promulgated by the Minister of National\nDefense and the Minister of the Budget."}},{"id":"PH-H19024-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"Funds needed to implement the Order shall be drawn from salary lapses and savings of the Integrated\nNational Police. Any further augmentation shall come from the Salary Adjustment Fund in the FY 1981\nGeneral Appropriations Act and from budgetary reserves. Funds intended to carry out this Order for the\nsucceeding years shall be incorporated in the annual appropriations of the INP."}},{"id":"PH-H19024-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"The salary increases authorized in this Order shall take effect August 8, 1981.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 10th day of September, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19025"] = {"id":"PH-H19025","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"}\\..~!ENDING l~PUBLr:C k~TI -SUBVERSION","orig":"}\\..~!ENDING l~PUBLr:C k~TI -SUBVERSION"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_1987.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_1987.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19025-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"follows:\n.,\n2.'\nPhi 1 i p pin est\nGovernment\nPhilippines-\nby force,\"'violence,\nsubversion\norganization\nsame purpose\nsuccessors\n~4;'~\n\" '\"\n,\n3.\n..\nPhilippines'\norganizations\nPhilippines\nsuccessors\norganizations.\"\n3\n4\naffiliates\nPhilippines,\nany subversive\nassociation\n.' s e c t ion s two\nt h r e e her e 0 f\nbe punished\npermanently\nappointive\nand elective,\nexercising\nconviction,\ncorreccional,\nsubsequent\nconvictions\nbe deported\nimmediately\nPhilippines\nany subversive\nassociation\nand thre-e.':hereof,\ns u c h me m' be r\nby prisionmayor\n~ndprovided,\n\n3/\nPhilippines\ngovernment\nsubdivisions\nsubversion\nbe punished\ncorreccional\n1700\nSEC..repealed.\n5 of Re;PUblic\n5.\nSEC.follows:\n-.\non confession\nSEC.diately.\n6.\neffect.irnme-\nand eighty-seven.\n/.(;,\nBy the President:"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19026"] = {"id":"PH-H19026","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":4,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES FORMALIZING INTER-AGENCY GUARANTEES (SIG) COMMITTEE FOR THE GRP-NDF PEACE TALKS","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES FORMALIZING INTER-AGENCY GUARANTEES (SIG) COMMITTEE FOR THE GRP-NDF PEACE TALKS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 4 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19026-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"Function.\nThe Committee\nshall be tasked to oversee the\nimplementation\nof the Joint Agreement on Safety and Immunity\nGuarantees\n(JASIG) and to resolve problems and issues arising from the same. The regular\npwticipatron\nof all principals is required to ensure faster decision-making\ncommunication\nof decisions to the field.\n'\nTo assist the Committee, a technical working group shall also be created\n.~\n.."}},{"id":"PH-H19026-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"Secretariat\nSecretariat support shall be provided by\nthe GRP Panel for CPPjNPAjNDF\nSecretariat."}},{"id":"PH-H19026-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Operational\nSUpport and Funding.\nOperational support and\nfunding shall be provided by the GRP Panel for CPPj NPAj NDF."}},{"id":"PH-H19026-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Effectivity.\nThis Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this\nday of September\nyear of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Nirlety-Five.\n.,..-\nBy the President:\n~f) serve as its technical arm comprised of senior representatives of the member"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19027"] = {"id":"PH-H19027","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MODIFYING THE NOMENCLATURE AND THE RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON VARIOUS PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION 104 OF THE TARIFF AND CUSTOMS CODE OF 1978 (PRESIDENTIAL DECREE NO. 1464, AS","orig":"BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES MODIFYING THE NOMENCLATURE AND THE RATES OF IMPORT DUTY ON VARIOUS PRODUCTS UNDER SECTION 104 OF THE TARIFF AND CUSTOMS CODE OF 1978 (PRESIDENTIAL DECREE NO. 1464, AS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_2000.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_2000.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19027-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The articles specifically listed in \"Annex A\" hereof, as classified under\nSection 1 04 of tile Tariff and Customs Code of 1978, as amended, shall be subject to the rates\nof import duty in accordance witIl the schedule indicated opposite each article."}},{"id":"PH-H19027-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 2"},"text":{"en":"The nomenclature and the rates of import duty on tariff headings not\nenumerated and those listed but represented by the symbol \"X X X\" shall renlain in force and"}},{"id":"PH-H19027-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 3"},"text":{"en":"Upon the effectivit), of this Executive Order. the articles specifically\nlisted in the aforesaid \"Annex\" which are entered or withdra\\vn from warehouses in the\nPhilippines for consumption shall be levied the rates of duty herein presented."}},{"id":"PH-H19027-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 4"},"text":{"en":"All other Presidential issuances, administrative rules and regulations, or\nparts thereof, which are inconsistent ,vith this Executive Order are hereby revoked or\nmodified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H19027-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 5"},"text":{"en":"This Executive Order shall take effect thirt), (30) days following the\ncomplete publication in hvo (2) newspapers of general circulation in the Philippines. .\nDone in the City of Manila, this ~ay\n' in the year of OUf\nLord Two Thousand.\n~\nBy the President\nRONALDO B. ZAMORA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19028"] = {"id":"PH-H19028","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG ANiS' LIBRARY. BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES IMPLEMENTING THE ENHANCED \"PCSO GREATER MEDICARE ACCESS","orig":"MALACAÑANG ANiS' LIBRARY. BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES IMPLEMENTING THE ENHANCED \"PCSO GREATER MEDICARE ACCESS"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 276","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00276_2004.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00276_2004.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19028-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 2"},"text":{"en":"PHILHEALTH. - Philhealth is hereby directed to:\na. Assist in the identification of indigent families and to target the\nenrollment of a total of five (5) million indigent families\nnationwide under the enhanced \"PCSO Greater Medicare\nAccess\" Program.\nPOMR Hologram • 24180\n\nb. Issue Philhealth Identification Cards to duly qualified\nbeneficiaries.\nc. Formulate and issue the Implementing Guidelines of this Order\nthrough a joint circular with PCSO.\nd. Perform all other acts necessary for the effective\nimplementation of the Program."}},{"id":"PH-H19028-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 3"},"text":{"en":"PCSO. - PCSO is hereby directed to:\na. Remit to Philhealth the LGU premium counterpart for duly\nqualified beneficiaries pursuant to the Implementing Guidelines\nof this Order.\nb. Help facilitate the identification and enrollment of qualified\nindigent families in coordination with local Social Welfare\nOfficers and/or the Punong Barangays and exert efforts\nnecessary to facilitate and expedite the same, consistent with\nexisting rules, procedures and guidelines.\nIssue appropriate resolutions, memoranda and office orders to\nformally adopt the enhanced \"PCSO Greater Medicare Access\"\nProgram and perform all other acts necessary to ensure its\nsmooth implementation.\nd. Formulate and issue the Implementing Guidelines of this Order\nthrough a joint circular with Philhealth."}},{"id":"PH-H19028-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 4"},"text":{"en":"Department of Budget and Mangement (DBM). - DBM is\nhereby directed to:\na. Allocate and facilitate the timely release of funds as payment for\nthe National Government (NG) premium counterpart to\nPhilhealth for the coverage of duly qualified beneficiaries.\nb. Perform all other acts necessary for the effective\nimplementation of the Program.\nPOMA Hologram * 24181\n3"}},{"id":"PH-H19028-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 5"},"text":{"en":"Department of Interior and Local Government (DILG) -\nDILG is hereby directed to:\na. Instruct all Punong Barangays to accomplish the list of\nbeneficiaries in accordance with the Implementing Guidelines of\nthe Program.\nb. Instruct its regional, provincial and municipal offices to mobilize\ntheir personnel to help the identification of beneficiaries, in\nconsultation with the Punong Barangays and to provide other\nsupport services as may be deemed necessary.\nc. Perform all other acts necessary for the effective\nimplementation of the Program."}},{"id":"PH-H19028-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 6"},"text":{"en":"Department of Health (DOH), Department of Agrarian\nReform (DAR), and Department of Social Welfare and Development\n(DSWD) - DOH, DAR and DSWD are hereby directed to:\na. Assist in the identification and enrollment of qualified indigent\nfamilies in the Program.\nb. Instruct their respective regional, provincial and municipal\noffices to mobilize their personnel to help in the identification of\nbeneficiaries, in consultation with the Punong Barangays and to\nprovide other support services as may be deemed necessary.\nc. Perform all other acts necessary for the effective\nimplementation of the Program.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect immediately.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this?9th day of January, in the year of Our\nLord, Two Thousand and Four.\nfloris hump\nBy the President:\nALBERTO G. ROMULO\nExecutive Secretary\nPOMA Hologram * 24182\n4"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19029"] = {"id":"PH-H19029","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA FE OUT OF A PORTION OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF PALO, PROVINCE OF LEYTE.","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES CREATING THE MUNICIPALITY OF SANTA FE OUT OF A PORTION OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF PALO, PROVINCE OF LEYTE."},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 277","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00277_1949.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00277_1949.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19029-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"OFFICIAL GAZETTE\nJuan, San Isidro, San Miguel, Tibak, and Pitogo, and the\nsitios of Badiangay, Bolod, Kilometer 17, and Curba, all of\nthe municipality of Palo, Province of Leyte, are hereby\norganized into an independent municipality, to be known\nas the municipality of Santa Fe, with the seat of govern-\nment at barrio Santa Fe.\nThe municipality of Palo shall have its present territory\nminus the portion thereof included in the municipality of\n'The municipality of Santa Fe, as herein organized, shall\nbegin to exist upon the appointment and qualification of\nthe mayor, vice-mayor, and a majority of the souncilors\nthereof, but in no case earlier than November 15, 1949.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 10th day of October,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and forty-nine,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the fourth.\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nPresident of the Philippines\n:4227\nBy the President:\nTEODORO EVANGELISTA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19030"] = {"id":"PH-H19030","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1957/eo_277_1957.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Providing for the Implementing Details for Reorganization Plan No. 1-A Relative to Position Classification","orig":"Providing for the Implementing Details for Reorganization Plan No. 1-A Relative to Position Classification"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 277","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1957-11-07","completenessNote":"全文，共 6 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00277_1957_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00277_1957_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19030-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"The authorized class titles of a position covered by the provisions of Reorganization Plan No.\n1-A shall be that appearing in the official allocation list prepared for each department and independent entity\nby the Wage and Position Classification Office, hereinafter referred to as “WAPCO.” Such class title shall be\nused for all official purposes and shall be binding on all administrative, certifying, payroll, disbursing,\naccounting, and auditing officers of the government."}},{"id":"PH-H19030-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"A position covered by the provisions of Reorganization Plan No. 1-A but not yet classified by\nthe WAPCO shall be described on the officially prescribed form and submitted to WAPCO for classification"}},{"id":"PH-H19030-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"en":"A full-time regular position created in the future and covered by the provisions of\nReorganization Plan No. 1-A shall be described on the officially prescribed form and submitted to WAPCO\nfor classification action. Such a position shall not be filled until receipt of notification of WAPCO\nclassification action."}},{"id":"PH-H19030-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"en":"Each department and independent entity shall” reflect the WAPCO class title beneath the current\ntitle of each item appearing in its July 1, 1956, staffing pattern in the column “Designation of Position,” and\nshall then furnish WAPCO a copy of such staffing pattern. On subsequent staffing pattern, only the WAPCO\nclass title shall appear in the column “Designation of Position.”"}},{"id":"PH-H19030-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"en":"Actions required by Reorganization Plan No. 1-A and these Implementing Details shall be\neffected within sixty days."}},{"id":"PH-H19030-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"en":"This Order shall take effect as of July 1, 1957.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 7th day of November, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nfifty-seven, and of the Independence of the Philippines, the twelfth.\n(Sgd.) CARLOS P. GARCIA\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\n(Sgd.) FORTUNATO DE LEON\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19031"] = {"id":"PH-H19031","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1970/eo_277_1970.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Creating the Presidential Advisory Committee on the Copper","orig":"Creating the Presidential Advisory Committee on the Copper"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 277","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1970-12-08","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00277_1970_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00277_1970_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19031-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 277, December 08, 1970 ]\nCREATING THE PRESIDENTIAL ADVISORY COMMITTEE ON THE COPPER INDUSTRY\nIn order to promote the orderly development of the copper industry and to hasten the further processing of\ncopper ores and concentrates into blister and refined copper products, and to protect the interests of the\ncountry in the long run, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers\nvested in me by law, do hereby establish and create the Presidential Advisory Committee on the Copper\nIndustry which shall be composed of the following members:\nFrom the Government:\n1. Chairman, Board of Investments\n2. Secretary of Finance or his representative\n3. Director, Bureau of Mines\nFrom the Private Sector:\nThe chief executives of the copper producing companies, or their authorized representatives"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
