  FT["PH-H19103"] = {"id":"PH-H19103","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑANG REORGANIZING THE METROPOLITAN WATERWORKS AND SYSTEM (MWSS) OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE NATIONAL, WATER CRISIS ACT OF 1995","orig":"MALACAÑANG REORGANIZING THE METROPOLITAN WATERWORKS AND SYSTEM (MWSS) OTHERWISE KNOWN AS THE NATIONAL, WATER CRISIS ACT OF 1995"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 286","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00286_1995.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00286_1995.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19103-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"Accordingly, the role of\nthe national government shall be to steer rather than row.\nshall, to the extent possible, encourage the private sector to\nparticipate in the delivery of public goods through franchising,\nconcession, management, privatization or other arrangements of the\nconcerned agencies operations or facilities.\nIN REPLYING, PLEASE CITE:\nPFVR Letter#\nTo ensure more effective and responsive delivery of\nwater services and increase revenues,\nService shall be divided into two Districts, each\nDistrict to be headed by a Deputy Administrator.\nEach District shall have four service areas with\neach Area (or department) performing the following\nfunctions, as well as such other functions that may\nbe assigned to it consistent with the purpose of\ndecentralizing to ensure better public service:\nGeneration,\ninstallation\ncollection\nFacilities\nImprovement\niii. Meter Management\nPublic Information\nreading, billing\nMaintenance\nThe Office of the Senior Administrator for Resource\nDevelopment and Management shall have direct\nsupervision over the\nAdministrators for\nEngineering and Construction, and for Administration\nand Finance.\nOffice of the Deputy Administrator for\nEngineering and\nConstruction shall undertake\nplanning and programming, monitoring, and evaluation\nof projects for the development and expansion of\nwaterworks and sewerage facilities.\nSpecifically,\nit shall have direct supervision over the following\ndepartments:\nProject Planning\nProject Design\nhi. Broiect Resignch and Quality Control\nThe same Deputy Administrator shall have direct\nsupervision over the Project Management\nwhich comprises\npresently consisting of five (5).\nproject managers,\n(f) The Office of the Deputy Administrator for Finance\nand Administration shall be responsible for resource\nmanagement and provision of administrative support\nIt shall consist of the following\ndepartments:\nAccounting\nManagerial Finance and Budget\niii. Human Resource\nDevelopment\nPrudence and restraint in the use of government resources\nshall be exercised.\nEfforts at streamlining and correcting\ndysfunctions in the operations and structures of the agencies\nconcerned shall be undertaken to achieve more with less.\ndelivery of more effective, efficient\nand responsible public\nservice shall be paramount.\nReorganization Plan for the MWSS.\nreorganized, as follows:\nThe MWSS shall be\nThe MWSS shall be headed by an Administrator\nwho shall be its chief executive officer.\nassisted by two (2) Senior Deputy Administrators, one for\nOperations and Customers Service and another for Resource\nDevelopment and Management.\nThere shall, moreover, be\nfour (4) Deputy Administrators, one (1) for Engineering\nand Construction,\none (1) for Finance and Administration,\ntwo (2) for Customers Service.\nThe Senior Deputy\nAdministrators and Deputy\nAdministrators shall be\nappointed by the Board, upon the recommendation of the\nAdministrator.\n2.2. Organization and Management.\nThe Administrator, with the\nassistance of his Senior Deputy Administrators, shall\nprovide over-all direction and control\noperations and administration of MWSS.\nThe Office of the Administrator shall have the\nfollowing services and/or departments directly under\nits supervision:\nCorporate Planning Service\nInternal Audit Service\niii. Management Information Service\nSystem Development Department\nComputer Service Department\nLegal Department\nvii. Public Affairs Department\nThe Office of the Senior Deputy Administrator for\nOperations and Customers Service shall be in charge\nof the operations and maintenance of the MWSS plants\nand other facilities, and the actual delivery of\nservice to water users.\nIt shall have direct\nsupervision of the following departments:\nWater Production\nWater Transmission and Meter Management\nGeneral Services\nPersonnel Management and Health Services\nThe Table of Organization down to department level\nis provided for in Annex A.\n2.3. Authority to Revise the Number of Departments.\nis, subject to the approval of the President,\nauthorized\nto revise the number of departments herein specified if\nand when the\nfranchising,\nsame becomes necessary by reason of a\nconcession, privatization\narrangements that will reduce the scope of its current\noperations and activities.\nreorganized, as follows:\nReorganization Plan for the LWA. The LWUA is hereby\nThe LWUA shall be headed by an Administrator\nwho shall be its chief executive officer.\nassisted by a Senior Deputy Administrator.\nThere shall,\nmoreover, be three\neach for Finance,\n(3) Deputy Administrators, one\n(1 )\nAdministration and Area Operations.\nAdministrators\nAdministrators shall be appointed by the Board, upon the\nrecommendation of the Administrator.\n3.2. Organization and Management.\nassistance of his Senior\nThe Administrator, with the\nprovide over-all\nDeputy Administrator, shall\ndirection and control\noperations and administration of the LWUA.\nThe Office of the Administrator shall have direct\nsupervision over the following departments:\nInternal Control\nManagement Services\niii. Public Affairs\nThe Office of the Senior Deputy Administrator shall\nhave direct supervision\ndepartments:\nSpecial Projects\niii. Water Resource Research and Training\nThe Senior Deputy Administrator shall also exercise\nsupervision\nAdministrators.\n(3)\nThe Office of the Deputy Administrator for Finance\nshall be responsible for financial\nmanagement and loans administration.\nSpecifically,\nit shall have direct supervision over the following\ndepartments:\nAccounting\niii. Loans Administration\nWater District Audit\nOffice of the Deputy\nAdministrator for\nAdministration shall be primarily responsible for\nthe provision of administrative services.\nhave direct supervision\nover the following\ndepartments:\nHuman Resource Management\nProperty Management\niii. General' Services\nThe Office of the Deputy Administrator for Area\nOperations shall have direct supervision over nine\n(9) area managers who will be responsible for the\nfollowing functions at the field level:\nProject Planning\nProject Monitoring and Evaluation\niii. Water District Development\nLoans Evaluation\n(E) The Table of Organization down to department level\nis provided for in Annex \"B\"\n3.3. Authority to Revise the Number of Departments.\nsubject to the approval of the President, authorized\nto revise the number of departments herein specified if\nand when the same becomes necessary\nfranchising, concession,\nby reason of\nprivatization\narrangements that will reduce the scope of its current\noperations and activities.\n4. Detailed Staffing.\ndirected to prepare their proposed detailed staffing\nThe MwsS and LWUA are hereby\npatterns accounting for all positions in the organization and the\ncorresponding budgetary and\nresource rearrangements\nThey are, moreover, required to conduct\npersonnel audit\ndetermine their respective\nrequirements.\nAn inventory of contracts of all contractual\nemployees including casual and temporary employees shall also be\nmade to determine the need for the continuation of their services.\nThe proposed staffing pattern shall be submitted to the\nDepartment of Budget and Management (DBM for review not later than\nsixty (60) days from the date hereof.\nThe DBM shall submit its\nrecommendation to the President within thirty (30)\nreceipt of the proposal but in no case later than ninety (90) days\nfrom the date hereof.\nThe revised staffing or manning pattern shall in no case\nexceed the number of existing authorized regular positions.\nRevised Compensation.\nhereby authorized to adopt\nclassification and compensation package\nemployees, subject to the following conditions:\nThe MWSS and the LWUA are\nand upgraded position\nfor its officers and\na. no diminution of the present salaries and benefits of\nMWSS and LWUA personnel;\nb. the revised rates of compensation shall be commensurate\nto the improved and efficient revenue collection of the\nagency concerned as determined by their respective Boards\nof Trustees;\nC. the adjusted rates shall not exceed industry and private\nsector rates of compensation;\napproval by the Board of Trustee of their respective\nbudgets which must be sufficient to cover the proposed\nadjustments on compensation;\nthe non-revenue water of the agency concerned shall in no\ncase be more than forty percent (40%); and\n£.\nfinal approval of the President.\nSeparation Pay. Any official or employee of the MWSS\nand LWUA who may be phased out by reason of the reorganization\nshall be entitled to such benefits as may be determined by existing\nFor this purpose, the MWSS, LWUA and DBM are hereby directed\nto study and propose schemes or measures to provide personnel who\nshall voluntarily retire from the service incentives and other\nbenefits, including the possibility of accelerating the application\nof the revised compensation package under the\nStandardization Law, Republic Act No. 6758.\nThe recommendation\nshould be submitted to the President not later than thirty (30)\ndays from the date hereof.\nEffectivity.\nThis Executive Order shall take effect\nthe day after its complete publication in a newspaper of general\ncirculation.\nDONE in the City of Manila, this 6th\nyear of Our Lord, Nineteen Hundred and Ninety-Five.\nday of December in the\nBy the Resident\nMETROPOLITAN WATERWORKS & SEWERAGE SYSTEM\nORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE\nBoard of Trustees\nAdministrator\nBoard Secretariat\nManagement\nInformation Service\nTechnology\nManagement\nDepartment\nDepartment\nDepartment\nSenior Deputy\nAdministrator for\nOperations &\nCustomer Service\nProduction\nDepartment\nWater Transmis\nManagement\nDepartment\nDepartment\nAdministrator for\nAdministrator for\nInternal Audit\nCorporate Planning\nPublic Affairs\nDepartment\nSenior Deputy\nAdministrator for\nResource Development\n& Management\nDeputy Administrator\nfor Engineering &\nConstruction\nPool of 5 Project\nDepartment\nDepartment\nApplied Research\n& Quality Control\nDepartment\nDeputy Administrator\nfor Administration &\nAccounting\nDepartment\nManagerial\nFinance & Budget\nDepartment\nDepartment\nHuman Resource\nDevelopment &\nManpower Plan-\nning Department\nGeneral Services\nDepartment\nManagement &\nHealth Services\nDepartment\nLOCAL WATER UTILITIES ADMINISTRATION\nORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE\nBoard of Trustees\nAdministrator\nPublic Affairs\nDepartment\nManagement\nServices Office\nInternal Control\nSenior Deputy\nAdministrator\nDepartment\nSpecial Projects\nWS Research &\nTraining Department\nDeputy Administrator\nfor Administration\nDeputy Administrator\nfor Finance\nDeputy Administrator\nfor Area Operations\nHuman Resource\nMgt. Department\nProperty Mgt.\nDepartment\nGeneral Services\nDepartment\nTreasury Department\nArea Managers (9)\nAccounting Department\nLoans Admin.\nDepartment\nWater District Audit\nDepartment"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
