  FT["PH-H19671"] = {"id":"PH-H19671","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 376","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 5 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00376_1950.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00376_1950.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19671-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The Rural Progress Administration creat-\ned by Executive Order No. 191, dated March 2, 1939,\npursuant to the provisions of Commonwealth Act No. 378,\nand converted into a corporation by Executive Order No.\n206, dated May 31, 1939, pursuant to the provisions of\nCommonwealth Act No. 378, as amended by Commonwealth\nActs Nos. 420 and 539, is hereby abolished, and its powers,\nduties and functions are hereby transferred to, vested in,\nand assumed by, the Bureau of Lands."}},{"id":"PH-H19671-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"There is hereby created in the Bureau of Lands\na Division of Landed Estates to handle the various phases\nof the activities presently undertaken by the Rural Pro-\ngress Administration. The Division of Landed Estates\nshall have the following positions and allotments for sundry\nexpenses and special purposes in lieu of those provided\nfor the Rural Progress Administration in its current prin-\ncipal budget:\nDIVISION OF LANDED ESTATES\nSALaries anD WAGES\n1. One chief of division\n2. One assistant\n5. One clerk-stenographer\n6. One clerk-typist\n7. One messenger\n4,800.00\n2,760.00\n2,580.00\n2,400.00\n1,680.00\n1,200.00\nSales and Collection Section\n8. One attorney\n9. One attorney\n10. One action clerk\n11. Three inspector-collectors at P2,160\n12. Three clerk-collectors at P2.160\n13. One clerk-collector\n11. One clerk-typist\n4,200.00\n3,120.00\n2,160.00\n•6,480.00\n6,480.00\n1,800.00\n1,680.00\nField Service Section\n15. One survevor\n16. Two assistant survevors at P2.160\n17. One superintendent\n18. Two superintendents at P3,120\n4,200.00\n4,320.00\n3,960.00\n6,240.00\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\n19. Three agents at P2.580\n20. One daftsman\n21. One computer\n22. One clerk-typist\n23: For temporary and emergency employees, includ-\ning, skilled, semi-skilled and unskilled laborers to be\nemployed from time to time\nTotal for salaries and wages\nSUNDRY EXPENSES\n1. Traveling expenses of personnel\n2. Freight, express and delivery service\n3. Postal, telegraph, telephone, cable and radio\n4. Illumination and power service\n5. Rental of bulidings and grounds .....\n6. Consumption of supplies and materials\n7. Printing and binding reports, documents, pam-\n8. Maintenance and repair on equipment\n9. Maintenance and repair of buildings\n10. Other services, including insurance premiums of\n11. Three per cent contribution of the Government\nfor the employees' insurance premiums in the Govern-\nment Service Insurance System\nTotal for sundry expenses\nSPECIAL PURPOSES\n1. For reimbursement to the Budget Commission\nfor the expenses of the accounting service\n(a) One accounting officer\n(6) One accountant\n(c) One bookkeeper\n(e) Four ledger clerks at P1,800\n(f) One janitor mesenger\n3,720.00\n2,580.00\n1,920.00\n7,200.00\n1,200.00\n2. For reimbursement to the General Auditing\nOffice for the expenses of the auditing service\n(a) One assistant auditör\n(b) One audit clerk\n2,580.00\n(c) One audit clerk\n1,920.00\n(d) One audit clerk\n• 1,680.00\n3. For the operation and maintenance of rice-mills,\nwarehouses and threshing machines\n(a) Buenavista Estate\n2,000.00\n5331\n2,580.00\n2,580.00\n1,680.00\n25,000.00\n1,000.00\n1,500.00\n500.00\n3,000.00\n6,000.00\n2.000.00\n1.000.00\n3,000.00\n9,500.00\n2,420.00\n10.140.00\n24.000.00\n\n5332\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\n4. For expenses in the administratir the Re-\nverend Crisostomo Estate\nTo be paid out of the Reverena vrisostomo\nDonation Fund\nSalaries and Weges\n(a) One clerk-collector\nTotal for salaries and\n(3,250.00)\nSundry Expenses\n(6) Traveling expenses of person-\n(c) Freight, express and delivery\n(d) Postal, telegraph, telephone,\ncable and radio service\n(e) Illumination and power service\n(f) Rental of buildings\n(g) Consumption of supplies and\n(h) Other services\n(i) Three ver cent contribution of\nthe Government for the em-\nployees' insurance premiums\nin the Government Service\nInsurance Syetem\nTotal for sundry expenses\nTotal for special purposes\n50.00\n20.00\n60.00\n360.00\n200.00\n100.00\n60.00\nTotal for salaries and wages .......\nTotal for sundry expenses\nTotal for special purposes\n37,920.00\n56,760.00\nSEc. 3. So much of the present personnel of the Rural\nProgress Administration as may be necessary and qualified\nshall be appointed in the Division of Landed Estates in\naccordance with the Civil Service Law, rules and regula-\ntions: PROVIDED, That any of the present personnel of the\nAdministration not so appointed in the Division of Landed\nEstates, unless he refuses to serve if retained, shall be\npaid from the funds of the Administration herein trans-\nferred and available for the purpose, gratuity in a lump\nsum equivalent to one month salary for every year of\ncontinuous satisfactory service rendered but not exceeding\n12 months, on the basis of the last salary received: PROVIDED,\nFURTHER, That any official or employee who has rendered\nless than one year of service shall be entitled to a gratuity\nof one-half of-one month's salary: AND PROVIDED, FINALLY,\nThat in case of subsequent reinstatement in the government\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nservice or in any government-owned or controlled corpora-\ntion, he shall refund to the National Government the value\nof the gratuity which he would not yet have received had it\nbeen paid to him in monthly installments."}},{"id":"PH-H19671-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"All the powers, duties and functions, records,\nproperties, equipment, assets, rights, choses in action, oblig-\nations and liabilities of the Rural Progress Administration\nabolished under this Order are hareby transferred to,\nand assumed by, the Bureau of Lands.\nSec. E. The proceeds from the sale of the estates hereto-\nfore administered by the Rural Progress Administration\nand any income derived from the administration of said\nestates shall constitute a special fund to be known as\nLanded Estates Fund which shall be used, subject to the\nprovisions of section 7-I (4) of Commonwealth Act No. 246,\nas amended, for operating expenses, for the settlement of\nthe liabilities and obligations of the Rural Progress\nAdministration and for the acquisition of private lands or\nany interest therein, through purchase ur expropriation,\nfor subdivision into home lots or small farms for resale at\nreasonable prices and under such conditions as may be fixed\nby the Secretary of Agriculture and Natural Resources to\ntheir bona fide tenants or occupants or to private individuals\nwho will work the lands themselves and who are qualified\nto acquire and own lands in the Philippines."}},{"id":"PH-H19671-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":"Commonwealth Act No. 378, as amended by\nCominonwealth Acts Nos. 420 and 539, and all acts or\nparts of acts and executive orders, administrative orders\nor parts thereof, which are inconsistent with the provisions\nof this Order, are hereby repealed or modified accordingly."}},{"id":"PH-H19671-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 7"},"text":{"en":"This Order shall take effect immediately.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 28th day of November,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty, and\nof the Independence of the Philippines, the fifth.\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nPresident of the Philipwines\n5333\nBy the President:\nTEODORO EVANGELISTA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19672"] = {"id":"PH-H19672","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1960/eo_376_1960.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Composition of the Armed Forces General Staff","orig":"Composition of the Armed Forces General Staff"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 376","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1960-02-10","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00376_1960_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00376_1960_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19672-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"The Armed Forces General Staff shall be organized into five Divisions, each under the direction\nof an Assistant Chief of Staff, as follows:\n(a) J-1, Personnel and Administrative Division\n(b) J-2, Intelligence Division\n(c) J-3, Organization, Operations, and Training Division\n(d) J-4, Logistics Division\n(e) J-5, Plans Division"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19673"] = {"id":"PH-H19673","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Conferring Cabinet Rank Uponthe Press Secretary","orig":"Conferring Cabinet Rank Uponthe Press Secretary"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 376","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1972-02-18","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00376_1972_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00376_1972_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19673-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 376 February 18, 1972\nCONFERRING CABINET RANK UPON THE PRESS SECRETARY\nBy virtue of the powers vested in me by law, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, do\nhereby elevate the Press Secretary to the rank of a member of the Cabinet, with rights, honors and privileges\npertaining to that position.\nExecutive Order No. 208, series of 1970, is hereby modified accordingly.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 18th day of February, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and\nseventy-two."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19674"] = {"id":"PH-H19674","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACANANG EXEcu'rIVE ORDER NO. 376 ESTABLISHING MONITORING EVALUATION OBJEC'rIVES, FORMULATION OPERATIONS AND FOR OTHER SIl'rDIAR PURPOSES","orig":"MALACANANG EXEcu'rIVE ORDER NO. 376 ESTABLISHING MONITORING EVALUATION OBJEC'rIVES, FORMULATION OPERATIONS AND FOR OTHER SIl'rDIAR PURPOSES"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 376","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00376_1989.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00376_1989.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19674-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"SEC 8"},"text":{"en":"Rescission Clause.\nAll orders, issuances, rules and\nregulations or parts thereof inconsistent with this Executive Order are\nhereby revoked or modified accordingly. However, this Executive Order\nshould complement Memorandum Order No. 175, as amended, which\nprovides for, among others, the creation of Project Monitoring Committees.\nEfrectivit~.\nThis Executive\nimmediately.\n\"\n\\!\n\\\nDONE in the City of Manila, .Philippines, this 2nd day of November in\nthe year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and eighty-nine.\n;'.~\nBy the President:\nCERTIFIED COPY~\n.\"'~';-\"'-';'-\"\": .,.-'.-.\nExecutive Secretary\nAURORA T. AOUINO\nPresidential Staff Director\nMalacanang Reco-,-ds Offj~"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
