  FT["PH-H19797"] = {"id":"PH-H19797","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MESSAGES   OF   THE   PRESIDENT","orig":"MESSAGES   OF   THE   PRESIDENT"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 397","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00397_1941.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00397_1941.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19797-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"OFFICIAL   GAZETTE\nQUEZON I  Vo/wine 4\nDone  at  the  City  of  Manila,  this  24th  day  of  December,  in  the  year  of  our  Lord,  nineteen\nhundred and forty-one, and of the Commonwealth of the Philippines, the seventh.\n(SGD.) MANUEL L. QUEZON\nBy the President:\n(SGD. ) TORGE 8. VARGAS\nSecretary to the President\nSot/roe.' Presidential Milseum and Library\nOffice  of the  President  of the  Philippines.  (1941).  /E#ecz4f!'„e  Order Nos...  33J  -400J.  Manila:\nPresidential Museum and Library."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19798"] = {"id":"PH-H19798","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":7,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE REORGANIZATION AND CON. VERSION OF THE PHILIPPINE LEGATIONS IN ROME, PARIS, AND MADRID INTO THE PHILIP- PINE EMBASSY IN MADRID, WITH CONCUR- RENT JURISDICTION OVER THE PHILIPPINE","orig":"MALACAÑAN PALACE BY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES PROVIDING FOR THE REORGANIZATION AND CON. VERSION OF THE PHILIPPINE LEGATIONS IN ROME, PARIS, AND MADRID INTO THE PHILIP- PINE EMBASSY IN MADRID, WITH CONCUR- RENT JURISDICTION OVER THE PHILIPPINE"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 397","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","completenessNote":"全文，共 7 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00397_1951.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00397_1951.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19798-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"SECTION 1"},"text":{"en":"The concurrent Philippine Legations in Rome,\nItaly and Paris, France and the Philippine Legation in\nMadrid, Spain are hereby reorganized and converted into\nthe Philippine Embassy in Madrid, with concurrent juris-\ndiction over the Philippine Legation in Rome and the con-\ncurrent Philippine Legations in Paris, the Vatican, Brussels\nand The Hague. The Embassy and the Legations shall\nhave their main offices in Madrid and Paris, respectively."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 2"},"text":{"en":"The combined appropriations amounting to Two\nhundred ninety-seven thousand, four hundred seventy-five\npesos (P297,475.00) authorized in Republic Act Numbered\nFive hundred sixty-three for\n(a) The Philippine Legation in Madrid, Spain\n(Item D-IV-7 (e), pages 78-80)\n(6) The concurrent Philippine Legations in Rome,\nItaly and Paris, France (Item D-IV-7 (f),\n165,725.00\nare hereby re-allotted for the operation and maintenance\nof the Philippine Embassy in Madrid, with concurrent\njurisdiction over the Philippine Legation in Rome, and\nthe concurrent Philippine Legation in Paris, the Vatican,\nBrussels and The Hague during the fiscal period from July\nfirst, nineteen hundred and fifty to June thirtieth, nineteen\nhundred and fifty-one, except as otherwise herein stated,\nPHILIPPINE EMBASSY IN MADRID, SPAIN\n(Diplomatic Post, Class I)\nSALARIES AND WAGES\nThe Ambassador\n1. The Ambassador at P12,000 for six months only\nSupplementary salary\n• Living quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n2. One foreign affairs officer, class II\nExcess of basic salary\nSupplementary salary\nLiving quarters allowance..\nPost allowance\n3. One foreign affairs officer, class III, at P6,000,\nfor seven months only (July 1, 1950 to Jan-\nSupplementary salary.\n3,000.00\n12,000.00\n6,000.00\n6,900.00\n300.00\n3,450.00\n4.800.00\n2;400.00\n3.500.00\n1,750.00\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n4. One commercial attache. (by detail)\nSupplementary salary\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n5. One administrative, finance and property of-\nSupplementary salary\n'6. One assistant at P4,800 for six months only.\n• Supplementary salary\n7. One assistant.\nSupplemental salary\n8. One interpreter-writer\n•Supplemental salary\n9. One. clerk-stenographer\nSupplemental salary\n10. One clerk-receptionist\nSupplemental salary\n11. One clerk-messenger\nSupplemental salary\n12. One chauffeur\nSupplemental salary\n13. One caretaker-janitor\nSupplemental salary\nPHILIFPINE LEGATION IN ROME, ITALY\n14. One foreign affairs officer, class III\nSupplemental salary\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n15. One administrative, finance and property of-\nSupplemental salary\nSupplemental salary\n17. One clerk-stenographer\nSupplemental salary\n18. One general utility clerk-helper\nSupplemental salary\n19. One. chauffeur\nSupplemental salary\nCONCURRENT PHILIPPINE LEGATION IN\nPARIS, THE VATICAN, BRUSSELS\nAND THE HAGUE\n20. The Minister\nSupplementary salary\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n21. • One foreign affairs officer, class II\nExcess of basic salary\nSupplementary salary\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n22. One foreign affffairs officer, class III\nSupplementary salary\nLiving quarters allowance\nPost allowance\n1,225.00\n3,750.00\n4.800.00\n2,400.00\n4,800.00\n2,400.00\n2,400.00\n600.00\n3.120.00\n2.280.00\n1,920.00\n2,280.00\n1,920.00\n2,880.00\n1,800.00\n1,200.00\n900.00\n300.00\n1,560.00\n840.00\n1.800.00\n600.00\n6.000.00\n3.000.00\n3,900.00\n2,100.00\n3,960.00\n2,040.00\n1,800.00\n1.200.00\n600.00\n420.00\n600.00\n240.00\n600.00\n240.00\n10,000.00\n5,000.00\n15,000.00\n.9,000.00\n6,900.00\n300.00\n3.450.00\n4,800.00\n2,400.00\n6.000.00\n3,000.00\n3,900.00\n2.100.00 -\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\n23. One administrative, finance and property of-\nSupplemental salary\n24. One assistant at P2,040 for six months (Jan-\nuary 1 to June 30, 1951)\nSupplemental salary\n25. One clerk-stenographer\nSupplemental salary\n26. One clerk-messenger\nSupplemental salary\n27. One chauffeur\nSupplemental salary\n28. One clerk-bookkeeper\nSupplemental salary\n29. One caretaker and general utility helper\nSupplemental salary\n3,060.00\n1,020.00\n1,380.00\n1,800.00\n3,000.00\n1,200.00\n600.00\n1.200.00\n600.00\n720.00\n480.00\n960.00\n480.00\nMISCELLANEOUS\n30. For. the employment of alien personnel as the\nneeds of the service may require\n31. Additional allowance for post, not exceeding\nP2,700 per annum, to the foreign affairs of-\nficer performing duties of charge d'Affaires in\n2,000.00\n2,700.00\nTotal for salaries and wages\nSUNDRY EXPENSES\n1. Traveling expenses of personnel\n2. Freight, express and delivery service\n3. Postal, telegraph, telephone, cable and radio\n4. Illumination and power service ......\n5. Rentals of buildings and grounds\n6. Consumption of supplies and materials\n7. Printing and binding reports, documents and\npublications\n8. Maintenance and repair of equipment\n9. Other services\n7,250.00\n3,500.00\n6,000.00\n1,100.00\n22,300.00\n8,000.00\n185.00\n1,500.00\n3,800.00\nTotal for sundry expenses ...\nFURNITURE AND EQUIPMENT\n1. For the purchase of furniture and equipment\n5.000.00\nTotal for furniture and equipment\nSPECIAL EXPENSES\n- 1. For representation expenses-\na. The Ambassador at P12,000 for six months\nonly (Jan. 1 to June 30, 1951)..\nb. The Minister\nc. Charge d'Affaires in Rome\n. 6,000.00\n9,000.00\n3,300.00\nTotal for representation expenses\nTotal for the Philippine Embassy in\nMadrid, with concurrent jurisdiction\nover the Philippine Legation in Rome\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nand the concurrent Philippine Legations\nin Paris, The Vatican; Brussels and\nand The Hague\nSEc. 3. Expenses incurred by the diplomatic offices here-\nin reorganized and established from July first, nineteen\nhundred and fifty up to thirty days from the date of the\npromulgation of this Order, the appropriations for which\nare not continued in this Order, shall be charged against\nthe respective appropriations authorized in Republic Act\nNumbered Five hundred sixty-three."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 4"},"text":{"en":"Any officer ur employee of the diplomatic offices\nherein reorganized and established whose position is\nabolished by virtue of this Order shall receive a gratuity\nin lump sun equivalent to one month salary for every\nyear of continuous and satisfactory service rendered but\nnot exceeding twelve months, on the basis of the last salary\nreceived: Provided, That any official or employee who has\nrendered less than one vear of service shall be entitled\nto a gratuity equivalent to one-half of one month's salary:\nAnd provided, fürther, That in case of subsequent re-\ninstatement in the government service or in any govern-\nment-owned or controlled corporation, he shall refund\nto the Nativnal Government the value of the gratuity\nwhich he would not. yet have received had it been paid\nto him in monthly installments."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 5"},"text":{"en":"The travelling expenses of personnel in the afore-\nmentioned diplomatic establishments whose positions are\nabolished or discontinued by this Order and of the im-\nmediate dependent members of their families, including\nexpenses for the shipment of their household effects, shall\nbe charged against the appropriation authorized in Re-\npublic Act Numbered Five hundred seventy-five, or from\nany saving in the appropriations for the Department of\nForeign Affairs."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 6"},"text":{"en":". All Acts, Executive Orders, Administrative\nOrders, Proclamations, and Department (of Foreign\nAffairs) Orders or parts thereof, inconsistent with any\nprovision of this Order are hereby repealed or modified\naccordingly: Provided, That the general provisions of Re-\npublic Act Numbered Five hundred sixty three and other\nActs or Orders applicable to the Foreign Service of the\nRepublic of the Philippines relative to the expenditure\nand disbursement of appropriations shall be applicable to\nthe appropriations herein re-allotted."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 7"},"text":{"en":"If any provision of this Order shall be held\ninvalid, the other provisions not affected thereby shall\nremain in full force and effect."}},{"id":"PH-H19798-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Sec 8"},"text":{"en":"This Order shall take effect as of July first,\nnineteen hundred and fifty, except as otherwise stated.\n\nOFFICIAL GAZETTE\nDone in the City of Manila, this 5th day of January,\nin the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and fifty-one,\nand of the Independence of the Philippines, the fifth.\nELPIDIO QUIRINO\nPresident of the Philippines\nBy the President:\nTEODORO EVANGELISTA\nExecutive Secretary"}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19799"] = {"id":"PH-H19799","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (HTML full text only)  |  https://lawphil.net/executive/execord/eo1960/eo_397_1960.html","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Opening Barrio Ayam in the Municipality of Limay, Province of Bataan, as Subport of Entry","orig":"Opening Barrio Ayam in the Municipality of Limay, Province of Bataan, as Subport of Entry"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 397","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1960-06-07","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00397_1960_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00397_1960_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19799-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"MALACAÑAN PALACE\nBY THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES\n[ EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 397, June 07, 1960 ]\nOPENING BARRIO AYAM IN THE MUNICIPALITY OF LIMAY, PROVINCE OF BATAAN, AS\nSUBPORT OF ENTRY\nWHEREAS, the Standard-Vacuum Refining Corporation (Philippines) is constructing its oil refinery in the\nmunicipality of Limay, province of Bataan;\nWHEREAS, the said corporation has requested the Philippine Government for facilities by opening barrio\nAyam in the vicinity of its refinery as a subport of entry for both foreign and coastwise trade; and\nWHEREAS, the establishment of such an oil refinery is a step forward in the industrial and economic\ndevelopment of the Philippines and will provide employment for a considerable number of technicians and\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, CARLOS P. GARCIA, President of the Philippines, pursuant to the provisions of\nsection 702 of Republic Act No. 1937 and upon the recommendation of the Secretary of Finance, do hereby\n1. The barrio of Ayam, municipality of Limay, province of Bataan, is hereby created, opened, and established\nas a subport of entry under Manila as the principal port of entry.\n2. The subport as herein created shall be furnished by the Government with only a skeleton force for customs\n3. The construction of the pier by the Standard-Vacuum Refining Corporation (Philippines) shall be subject to\nthe supervision of the Department of Public Works and Communications.\n4. The Bureau of Customs shall collect the corresponding wharfage dues and berthing charges pursuant to\nRepublic Act No. 1937, as amended."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
  FT["PH-H19800"] = {"id":"PH-H19800","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"The LawPhil Project — Arellano Law Foundation","sourceUrl":"LawPhil (source has HTML full text only)","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":1,"structureMode":"WHOLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"Extending the Term ofthe Presidential Commission on Reorganization Created Under Executive Order No. 281, S. 1970","orig":"Extending the Term ofthe Presidential Commission on Reorganization Created Under Executive Order No. 281, S. 1970"},"level":"law","status":"active","docNumber":"Executive Order No. 397","issuingBody":"President of the Philippines","promulgatedDate":"1972-06-27","completenessNote":"全文，共 1 条；逐字取自 LawPhil PDF 文本化成果（第三方 OCR，非机翻），原始文件 EO_00397_1972_html.txt","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"菲律宾/法律原文/07_行政命令_EO/EO_00397_1972_html.txt","country":"PH","countryName":"菲律宾","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"PH-H19800-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{},"text":{"en":"EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 397 June 27, 1972\nEXTENDING THE TERM OF THE PRESIDENTIAL COMMISSION ON REORGANIZATION\nCREATED UNDER EXECUTIVE ORDER NO. 281, S. 1970\nWHEREAS, the Integrated Reorganization Plan has already been submitted to Congress last March 4, 1972,\npursuant to Section 4 of Republic Act No. 5435, as amended;\nWHEREAS, it is desirable to maintain the active involvement of the members of the Presidential Commission\non Reorganization in the consideration of the Integrated Reorganization Plan by Congress and in its eventual\napproval; and\nWHEREAS, it is necessary that the Commission undertake such informational activities as may be necessary\nto ensure wider understanding and support of the reorganization proposals;\nNOW, THEREFORE, I, FERDINAND E. MARCOS, President of the Philippines, by virtue of the powers\nvested in me by law, do hereby extend the term of the Presidential Commission on Reorganization and the\nnecessary technical staff thereof, from July 1, 1972 to September 30, 1972, to perform the following:\n1. Participate and render such technical assistance as may be required by Congress in its consideration of the\nIntegrated Reorganization Plan;\n2. Act as liaison and render such services for the Office of the President as may be necessary to ensure the\napproval of the reorganization plan by Congress;\n3. Undertake such informational activities as may be necessary to ensure wider understanding and support of\nthe reorganization proposals; and\n4. Perform such other functions as may be necessary to accomplish the foregoing objectives.\nThe Executive Secretary shall issue the necessary directives to the other government agencies with personnel\ndetailed to the Commission for the extension of the detail of such personnel whose services may still be\nneeded by the Commission.\nThe Commission is authorized to disburse and defray all expenses for its operations from July 1 to September\n30, 1972 and avail of funds that shall be provided for it under a special budget in the Office of the President,\nincluding compensation of all the regular personnel. The Commission is also authorized to grant to the\npersonnel of the technical staff whose detail are extended from other government offices as well as those who\nmay be on consultancy basis from the private sector, including the members of the Commission honorarium\nand/or allowances in such reasonable amounts as it may determine.\nDone in the City of Manila, this 27th day of June, in the year of Our Lord, nineteen hundred and seventy-two."}}],"pack":"ph-p158"};
